{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content C:/Users/malgh/.codex/skills/personal-workstyle/references/profile.md; Get-Content firmware/family/include/services/settings.h; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_store.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_cal.c'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content C:/Users/malgh/.codex/skills/personal-workstyle/references/profile.md; Get-Content firmware/family/include/services/settings.h; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_store.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_cal.c'","aggregated_output":"# Evolving Collaboration Profile\r\n\r\nLast reviewed: 2026-10-04\r\n\r\nThis file stores durable, evidence-backed working principles. Re-verify changing environment facts before relying on them.\r\n\r\n## Core Objective\r\n\r\n- Build a coherent personal AI operating system rather than isolated one-off fixes.\r\n- Use subscriptions, local hardware, free or inexpensive models, tools, and agents as complementary resources.\r\n- Optimize for real end-to-end usefulness: discoverable, callable, tested, maintainable, and understandable in the interface.\r\n\r\n## Request Understanding\r\n\r\n- Treat consecutive messages and side questions as connected branches of one evolving intent unless the user clearly replaces the request.\r\n- Maintain coverage of every meaningful branch. Do not drop an earlier question because a newer technical issue appeared.\r\n- Look beyond literal wording when corrections reveal a larger system goal, but do not invent a materially different objective.\r\n- Clarifications often refine the standard of success rather than replace the task.\r\n\r\n## Decision Principles\r\n\r\n- Prefer evidence from the actual device, configuration, UI, logs, and live tests over confident assumptions.\r\n- For removable or external storage, verify the physical disk identity (such as serial number and unique ID) before destructive work; never rely on a drive letter alone.\r\n- Keep these distinctions explicit: app versus CLI; installed versus discovered; discovered versus callable; callable versus tested; tested versus dependable.\r\n- Evaluate solutions at the user's likely scale. A method suitable for hundreds of items may be unsuitable for tens of thousands.\r\n- Route high-volume deterministic work to local tools and hardware where practical; reserve expensive model reasoning for ambiguity, judgment, planning, and review.\r\n- Prefer reusable shared capabilities when several agents can benefit, but account for each platform's discovery paths and compatibility rather than assuming one folder works everywhere.\r\n- Avoid unnecessary downloads, duplicated integrations, and configuration clutter. Install or retain components when their expected recurring value exceeds their maintenance and storage cost.\r\n- Prefer the minimum sufficient workflow for straightforward organization tasks. Do not turn a simple folder plan into a broad metadata, evidence, and review system unless that extra structure has a clear requested benefit.\r\n- Isolate experimental providers, models, and API routes from the stable default interface until their behavior, pricing, and discovery are verified.\r\n- For bulk or risky changes, favor preview, sample, verification, resumable batches, logs, rollback, and cleanup in proportion to the risk.\r\n- A strong orchestrator should own planning and review; cheaper, free, local, or specialized agents may execute bounded work when that genuinely saves time or usage.\r\n- Select worker models dynamically from current capabilities: the smallest capable model for routine work, a mid-tier model for bounded work requiring more judgment, and the primary agent for difficult or safety-critical decisions and final review. Set each worker's model and reasoning effort explicitly; never inherit the primary agent's expensive model by default.\r\n- Do not spawn same-tier high-end sub-agents without an explicit user-requested or approved exception. If lighter workers are unavailable or inadequate, narrow the task or do it directly. Avoid full-history forks that force expensive model inheritance. This rule is also saved independently of this skill in the global Codex AGENTS.md; its local scope does not establish account-wide synchronization.\r\n- Do not delegate a trivial task when briefing, context duplication, retries, and final review are likely to cost more time or model usage than doing it directly. Treat subagents primarily as a way to parallelize cleanly independent work or apply a useful specialization, not as an automatic usage-saving mechanism.\r\n- Treat a capable delegated model such as Ox as a peer reviewer for substantial plans when requested, not merely as a cheap substitute worker. Temporary model unavailability should not block deterministic local inventory or hashing.\r\n- Delegation does not transfer responsibility. Inspect the actual output, diff, or artifact and rerun meaningful checks.\r\n- When delegated model usage is materially cheaper or separately metered, prefer a different fresh worker session for the first independent review, then reserve the main model for disagreements, high-risk cases, and a sentinel sample. Never let the proposing conversation approve its own output.\r\n- When the user explicitly accepts a known risk, respect that decision and proceed within scope. Do not repeatedly relitigate the same accepted risk.\r\n- State source and maturity accurately: upstream, custom, experimental, contract-tested, live-tested, or inferred.\r\n- When reviewing a received project (vendor or third-party deliverable), only the received artifacts, external reference documents, and what the user states in chat count as facts. Notes, reviews and \"context\" files written by earlier agents are unverified inference, even inside CLAUDE.md. Never repeat an agent-written claim about people, agreements or management decisions as fact; re-verify technical claims against the source and label provenance.\r\n- When the work is for a third party who cannot steer an agent, deliver a briefed autonomous agent rather than an automation script. Encode the mission, the decision rules, the already-learned environment facts, the verification standard, and an explicit list of what may be asked of that person â€” reducing their involvement to logins and yes/no answers. A script only covers the steps already anticipated; a brief lets the agent handle discovery and surprises.\r\n- When installing third-party integrations on someone else's working machine, prefer first-party vendor packages, read the actual source before trusting a community project, pin a version, and install nothing at all rather than the least-bad candidate. Never modify that person's professional software or licences.\r\n\r\n## Communication\r\n\r\n- Default to clear Egyptian Arabic, using familiar English technical terms when they are shorter or more precise.\r\n- Lead with the outcome and explain only the technical detail needed to evaluate the decision.\r\n- Do not confuse brevity with incompleteness. Cover all important branches without padding.\r\n- Distinguish fact, inference, recommendation, and confirmed test result.\r\n- If an earlier claim or implementation was wrong, say what was wrong, correct it, and explain the practical effect.\r\n- Treat screenshots and user verification as evidence that can overturn earlier assumptions.\r\n\r\n## Collaboration Behavior\r\n\r\n- Continue useful in-scope work while discussing related questions when the environment and instructions permit it.\r\n- Use parallel work or delegation when the user requests it or the active rules permit it and the tasks are genuinely independent.\r\n- Ask for clarification only when a missing choice would materially change the result or authority; otherwise make a reasonable, disclosed assumption.\r\n- Prefer a clean architecture and source of truth over several overlapping paths that create uncertainty about which one is active.\r\n\r\n## Known Architecture â€” Verify Before Relying\r\n\r\n- Codex is the preferred final reviewer for consequential merges/execution when requested, but a validated external supervisor such as OpenCode/Ox may own long-running bounded queues and coordinate cheaper vision workers between checkpoints.\r\n- External or free models should normally be isolated workers rather than silently replacing the main subscribed model.\r\n- A direct isolated Ox/OpenRouter delegate has been live-tested; a globally exposed custom provider previously caused model-list clutter and an unsupported ChatGPT-account route.\r\n- OpenCode CLI 1.18.23 and `opencode-delegate` 0.5.0 are installed and discoverable. Global delegation lanes `ox` â†’ `openrouter/stealth/ox-alpha` and `hy3` â†’ `opencode/hy3-free` are validated and resolvable. The OpenRouter environment credential exposes Ox Alpha, and a direct read-only CLI smoke test returned `OX_OK` at zero reported cost. OpenCode's credential file itself currently lists zero stored credentials, so re-check the environment credential before future delegation.\r\n- Antigravity CLI 1.2.14 is installed and authenticated; its model list includes Gemini 3.8/3.7/3.6 Flash, Gemini 3.1 Pro, Claude 4.6, and GPT-OSS labels. The shared `agy-delegate` 0.6.0-local relay now prepares per-project grants using BOM-free JSON at `~/.gemini/config/projects/<uuid>.json`, nested `permissionGrants.permissionGrants.allow/deny`, and a reusable workspace registry. This was live-tested with global grants removed, paths containing spaces, and installed project reuse. Shell/interpreter grants are approvals, not filesystem confinement. On Windows agy 1.2.14, `--sandbox --dangerously-skip-permissions` persisted a write-tool change: never claim it enforces read-only there. The relay uses plan mode without bypass on Windows, reports denied tools honestly, and fails detected read-only changes. Prior versions' path/permission failures must be rechecked before applying historical workarounds. The shared 15-second startup gate remains; the separate media supervisor's previously tested six-process cap and source-read-only workflow were not retested in this change.\r\n- Desktop applications being present does not prove their automation CLI is installed or discoverable.\r\n- Reviews of received projects use the `review-workspace` skill (central store `~/.agents/skills`, junctioned into Claude and Codex). It has two layers: a tagged English work layer for agents and engineers, and an Arabic understanding layer `_ÙÙ‡Ù…/` for the user (explanations, diagrams, interactive pages), which is not in git and is never a source. The user prefers to learn a received project through plain-language pages he can play with, not by reading the agents' working files.\r\n- Hermes delegation should resolve the strongest model currently configured as Hermes's default instead of hard-coding a legacy model ID; the current verified default is `hy3-free`. Treat vision as a separate capability check: in the present setup `hy3-free` has no native vision and the auxiliary vision route returns HTTP 401.\r\n- The shared MediaOrganizer virtual environment currently uses Python 3.10.11; keep its scripts free of Python 3.11-only APIs and test them with that interpreter.\r\n- The user's own projects in `D:\\tasks` share one working system: `AGENTS.md` is the entry point for every agent (`CLAUDE.md` only imports it), `STATE.md` is read second and updated last and is the hand-off between sessions, accounts and agents, plus `ISSUES.md`, MADR `decisions/`, dated never-edited evidence, and \"no claim without the report\". Any Claude Code mod, hook or automation must reinforce that system, never add a parallel state file or a new file in `docs/`, and never be the only guard, because Codex, agy and other agents do not run Claude Code mods.\r\n- The user alternates the same projects between two Claude subscriptions on one login (Team org and a personal Pro org) when a usage limit runs out; transcripts of both are stored locally under `~/.claude/projects`, tagged by `organizationUuid`. Each session stays on the account it was started on. Usage-limit safe points (finish the step, update `STATE.md`, stop) are a recurring need across every session, not one conversation.\r\n\r\n## Do Not Preserve\r\n\r\n- Credentials, tokens, secrets, or private file contents.\r\n- Temporary project choices or transient UI state.\r\n- Task-specific naming, formatting, or style choices unless the user explicitly makes them general.\r\n- Sensitive personal traits or speculative interpretations of personality.\r\n#ifndef FAMILY_SETTINGS_H\r\n#define FAMILY_SETTINGS_H\r\n#include \"common/types.h\"\r\n#include \"common/fault_codes.h\"\r\n#include <stddef.h>\r\n\r\n#define SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE 768u\r\n#define CAL_SLOT_SIZE 256u\r\n#define CAL_MISSING INT32_MAX\r\ntypedef struct {\r\n    ch_type_t type;\r\n    ch_mode_t mode;\r\n    char name[6];\r\n    temp_dC_t alarm_dC, trip_dC, probe_limit_dC;\r\n    uint8_t band_C, type_epoch;\r\n} chan_cfg_t;\r\ntypedef struct {\r\n    uint8_t board_type, channel_count, address, baud;\r\n    uint16_t pin_bcd;\r\n    uint32_t sequence;\r\n    chan_cfg_t ch[MAX_CHANNELS];\r\n} settings_t;\r\ntypedef struct {\r\n    uint8_t bank_count;\r\n    uint32_t sequence;\r\n    int32_t ref_ppm[MAX_BANKS], baseline_nV[MAX_CHANNELS];\r\n    uint8_t tag[MAX_CHANNELS];\r\n} calibration_t;\r\n\r\n/* Pure, whole-record semantic validation; no defaults or partial acceptance. */\r\nres_t set_validate(const settings_t *s);\r\nuint16_t set_crc16(const uint8_t *p, size_t n);\r\n/* Slots are little endian; trailing bytes are zero; unpack checks build identity. */\r\nres_t set_pack(const settings_t *s, uint8_t out[SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE]);\r\nres_t set_unpack(const uint8_t in[SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE], uint8_t board_type,\r\n                 uint8_t channel_count, settings_t *s);\r\n/* -1 neither valid, 0 A, 1 B; equal/half-range sequences deterministically prefer A. */\r\nint set_select(bool a_valid, uint32_t a_seq, bool b_valid, uint32_t b_seq);\r\nbool set_protection_changed(const settings_t *a, const settings_t *b);\r\n/* Edit helper: increments epoch on a change, clears limits; OFF is canonical. */\r\nres_t set_change_type(chan_cfg_t *c, ch_type_t type);\r\nres_t cal_validate(const calibration_t *c);\r\nres_t cal_pack(const calibration_t *c, uint8_t out[CAL_SLOT_SIZE]);\r\nres_t cal_unpack(const uint8_t in[CAL_SLOT_SIZE], uint8_t banks, calibration_t *c);\r\n/* Staged records may validate but must be complete and type/epoch-bound to run. */\r\nbool cal_complete(const calibration_t *c, const settings_t *s);\r\n/* All-or-nothing burnout update, absolute window 1.5..10 mV. */\r\nres_t cal_learn(calibration_t *c, const settings_t *s,\r\n                const int32_t baseline_nV[MAX_CHANNELS]);\r\n\r\ntypedef enum { STORE_IDLE, STORE_INVALIDATE, STORE_BODY, STORE_MAGIC,\r\n               STORE_VERIFY, STORE_DONE, STORE_FAILED } store_phase_t;\r\ntypedef enum { EE_NONE, EE_WRITE, EE_READ } ee_kind_t;\r\ntypedef struct { ee_kind_t kind; uint16_t address; uint8_t value; } ee_op_t;\r\ntypedef struct {\r\n    store_phase_t phase;\r\n    uint8_t image[SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE];\r\n    uint8_t wrap_cal_image[CAL_SLOT_SIZE];\r\n    uint16_t length, index, base;\r\n    uint8_t active_slot, target_slot, retries;\r\n    bool pending, protection_change, calibration;\r\n    bool settings_after_cal;\r\n    uint8_t calibration_active_slot;\r\n    bool calibration_slot_known;\r\n    fault_code_t fault;\r\n} set_store_t;\r\n/* Initialize once per boot. Do not reinitialize to retry a failed commit. */\r\nvoid set_store_init(set_store_t *st);\r\n/* Begin rejects invalid RAM data; sequence is active+1. Caller must inhibit RUN\r\n * BEFORE executing the first emitted operation if protection_change is true.\r\n * active_slot = 0/1, or 2 for blank EEPROM. No settings pointer flip until STORE_DONE.\r\n * An in-progress transaction returns RES_BUSY; failures survive a new attempt. */\r\nres_t set_commit(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate,\r\n                 const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot);\r\n/* Required for a type-epoch wrap; plain set_commit rejects that change.\r\n * Copies the active calibration (valid staged records allowed; slot 0/1), clears\r\n * every wrapping channel's baseline/tag, and verifies its inactive A/B copy BEFORE\r\n * writing settings. image remains the pending settings image; calibration=true\r\n * during the prerequisite write. active_slot is the SETTINGS slot throughout;\r\n * calibration_active_slot advances after calibration verification. STORE_DONE\r\n * means both records verified; no caller-owned input must survive begin.\r\n * Retries must pass that verified slot and its calibration record; a stale\r\n * calibration slot is rejected. Keep this store state across attempts.\r\n * On reset, boot-select both A/B pairs normally. A cut can leave old settings\r\n * with a newly cleared baseline (requiring re-learning), never wrapped settings\r\n * with the ancient baseline. Non-wrapping saves follow set_commit unchanged. */\r\nres_t set_commit_with_cal(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate,\r\n                          const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot,\r\n                          const calibration_t *active_cal, uint8_t cal_slot);\r\n/* Also rejects a stale calibration slot once this store has verified a copy. */\r\nres_t cal_commit(set_store_t *st, const calibration_t *candidate,\r\n                 uint32_t active_sequence, uint8_t active_slot);\r\n/* Pure EEPROM protocol: execute op once; next call acknowledges it with ready,\r\n * success and (for EE_READ) value. ready=false preserves the outstanding op.\r\n * At most one byte request per call. Fault stays raised until successful retry. */\r\nvoid set_store_step(set_store_t *st, bool ready, bool success, uint8_t value,\r\n                    ee_op_t *op);\r\n#endif\r\n#include \"services/settings.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\nvoid set_store_init(set_store_t *st)\r\n{\r\n    if(st!=NULL) { memset(st,0,sizeof(*st)); st->active_slot=2; st->calibration_active_slot=2; }\r\n}\r\nstatic bool available(const set_store_t *st)\r\n{ return st->phase==STORE_IDLE || st->phase==STORE_DONE || st->phase==STORE_FAILED; }\r\nstatic void begin(set_store_t *s, uint8_t active, uint16_t size, bool cal, bool prot)\r\n{\r\n    s->phase=STORE_INVALIDATE; s->active_slot=active;\r\n    s->target_slot=active==0?1:0;\r\n    s->base=(uint16_t)(cal?(0x640u+256u*s->target_slot):(0x40u+768u*s->target_slot));\r\n    s->length=size; s->index=2; s->pending=false; s->retries=0;\r\n    s->calibration=cal; s->protection_change=prot;\r\n    s->settings_after_cal=false;\r\n    if(cal) { s->calibration_active_slot=active; s->calibration_slot_known=true; }\r\n}\r\nstatic res_t settings_commit(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate,\r\n                             const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot,\r\n                             const calibration_t *cal, uint8_t cal_slot)\r\n{\r\n    settings_t next; calibration_t next_cal; uint8_t i; bool wraps=false;\r\n    if(st==NULL || active_slot>2 || set_validate(candidate)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(!available(st)) return RES_BUSY;\r\n    if(active!=NULL) {\r\n        if(active_slot>1 || set_validate(active)!=RES_OK || candidate->board_type!=active->board_type ||\r\n           candidate->channel_count!=active->channel_count) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        /* Epoch changes are enforced at the commit boundary, not trusted to UI. */\r\n        for(i=0;i<active->channel_count;++i) {\r\n            uint8_t expected=active->ch[i].type_epoch;\r\n            if(active->ch[i].type!=candidate->ch[i].type) expected=(uint8_t)((expected+1u)&63u);\r\n            if(candidate->ch[i].type_epoch!=expected) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n            if(active->ch[i].type_epoch==63 && expected==0) wraps=true;\r\n        }\r\n    } else if(active_slot!=2) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(wraps) {\r\n        uint8_t banks=candidate->board_type==40?6u:(uint8_t)(candidate->channel_count/8u);\r\n        if(cal_slot>1 || cal_validate(cal)!=RES_OK || cal->bank_count!=banks) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        /* A settings verification failure may leave its copy boot-selectable.\r\n         * Never overwrite the verified cleared calibration using a stale slot\r\n         * on retry: that would briefly expose the ancient baseline again. */\r\n        if(st->calibration_slot_known && cal_slot!=st->calibration_active_slot) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        next_cal=*cal; next_cal.sequence=cal->sequence+1u;\r\n        for(i=0;i<active->channel_count;++i)\r\n            if(active->ch[i].type_epoch==63 && candidate->ch[i].type_epoch==0) {\r\n                next_cal.baseline_nV[i]=CAL_MISSING; next_cal.tag[i]=0;\r\n            }\r\n        if(cal_pack(&next_cal,st->wrap_cal_image)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    }\r\n    next=*candidate; next.sequence=active?active->sequence+1u:0;\r\n    if(set_pack(&next,st->image)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    begin(st,active_slot,(uint16_t)(18u+16u*next.channel_count),false,set_protection_changed(active,&next));\r\n    if(wraps) {\r\n        begin(st,cal_slot,249,true,true);\r\n        st->active_slot=active_slot; st->settings_after_cal=true;\r\n    }\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nres_t set_commit(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate, const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot)\r\n{\r\n    return settings_commit(st,candidate,active,active_slot,NULL,2);\r\n}\r\nres_t set_commit_with_cal(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate,\r\n                          const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot,\r\n                          const calibration_t *active_cal, uint8_t cal_slot)\r\n{\r\n    return settings_commit(st,candidate,active,active_slot,active_cal,cal_slot);\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_commit(set_store_t *st, const calibration_t *candidate, uint32_t active_sequence, uint8_t active_slot)\r\n{\r\n    calibration_t next;\r\n    if(st==NULL || active_slot>2 || cal_validate(candidate)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(!available(st)) return RES_BUSY;\r\n    if(st->calibration_slot_known && active_slot!=st->calibration_active_slot) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    next=*candidate; next.sequence=active_slot==2?0:active_sequence+1u;\r\n    if(cal_pack(&next,st->image)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    begin(st,active_slot,249,true,true); return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nstatic void retry_or_fail(set_store_t *s)\r\n{\r\n    s->pending=false;\r\n    if(s->fault!=FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT) s->fault=s->protection_change?FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT:FC_G13_SAVE_FAIL_INFO;\r\n    if(s->retries==0) { s->retries=1; s->phase=STORE_INVALIDATE; s->index=2; }\r\n    else s->phase=STORE_FAILED;\r\n}\r\nstatic const uint8_t *store_image(const set_store_t *s)\r\n{ return s->settings_after_cal?s->wrap_cal_image:s->image; }\r\nvoid set_store_step(set_store_t *s, bool ready, bool success, uint8_t value, ee_op_t *op)\r\n{\r\n    if(op==NULL) return;\r\n    memset(op,0,sizeof(*op));\r\n    if(s==NULL || !ready) return;\r\n    if(s->phase==STORE_IDLE || s->phase==STORE_DONE || s->phase==STORE_FAILED) return;\r\n    if(s->pending) {\r\n        s->pending=false;\r\n        if(!success || (s->phase==STORE_VERIFY && value!=store_image(s)[s->index])) retry_or_fail(s);\r\n        else switch(s->phase) {\r\n        case STORE_INVALIDATE: s->phase=STORE_BODY; s->index=2; break;\r\n        case STORE_BODY:\r\n            ++s->index;\r\n            if(s->index==s->length) { s->phase=STORE_MAGIC; s->index=1; }\r\n            break;\r\n        case STORE_MAGIC:\r\n            if(s->index==1) s->index=0;\r\n            else { s->phase=STORE_VERIFY; s->index=0; }\r\n            break;\r\n        case STORE_VERIFY:\r\n            ++s->index;\r\n            if(s->index==s->length) {\r\n                if(s->settings_after_cal) {\r\n                    uint8_t settings_slot=s->active_slot, cal_slot=s->target_slot;\r\n                    begin(s,settings_slot,(uint16_t)(18u+16u*s->image[4]),false,true);\r\n                    s->calibration_active_slot=cal_slot;\r\n                } else {\r\n                    s->phase=STORE_DONE; s->active_slot=s->target_slot;\r\n                    if(s->calibration) s->calibration_active_slot=s->target_slot;\r\n                    if(s->fault!=FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT || s->protection_change) s->fault=FC_NONE;\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n            break;\r\n        default: retry_or_fail(s); break;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    switch(s->phase) {\r\n    case STORE_INVALIDATE: op->kind=EE_WRITE; op->address=s->base; op->value=0; break;\r\n    case STORE_BODY: case STORE_MAGIC:\r\n        op->kind=EE_WRITE; op->address=(uint16_t)(s->base+s->index); op->value=store_image(s)[s->index]; break;\r\n    case STORE_VERIFY: op->kind=EE_READ; op->address=(uint16_t)(s->base+s->index); break;\r\n    case STORE_DONE: case STORE_FAILED: case STORE_IDLE: return;\r\n    default: s->phase=STORE_FAILED; s->fault=FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT; return;\r\n    }\r\n    s->pending=true;\r\n}\r\n#include \"services/settings.h\"\r\n#include \"settings_bytes.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\n\r\nuint16_t set_crc16(const uint8_t *p, size_t n)\r\n{\r\n    uint16_t crc=0xFFFF;\r\n    size_t i; uint8_t bit;\r\n    if(p==NULL || n>SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE) return 0;\r\n    for(i=0;i<n;++i) {\r\n        crc^=(uint16_t)((uint16_t)p[i]<<8);\r\n        for(bit=0;bit<8;++bit)\r\n            crc=(uint16_t)((crc&0x8000u)?((uint16_t)(crc<<1)^0x1021u):(uint16_t)(crc<<1));\r\n    }\r\n    return crc;\r\n}\r\nres_t set_validate(const settings_t *s)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i, j, fitted=0;\r\n    if(s==NULL) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(!((s->board_type==8 && s->channel_count==8) ||\r\n         (s->board_type==24 && s->channel_count==24) ||\r\n         (s->board_type==40 && s->channel_count==43))) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(s->address<1 || s->address>247 || s->baud>1) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<4;++i) if(((s->pin_bcd>>(4u*i))&15u)>9u) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) {\r\n        const chan_cfg_t *c=&s->ch[i]; int16_t max;\r\n        for(j=0;j<6;++j) if((uint8_t)c->name[j]<0x20 || (uint8_t)c->name[j]>0x7E) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        if(c->type_epoch>63 || (c->mode!=CH_MODE_TRIP && c->mode!=CH_MODE_ALARM_ONLY)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        switch(c->type) {\r\n        case CH_TYPE_OFF:\r\n            if(c->mode!=CH_MODE_TRIP || c->alarm_dC!=0 || c->trip_dC!=0 ||\r\n               c->band_C!=2 || c->probe_limit_dC!=0) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n            continue;\r\n        case CH_TYPE_K: max=13720; break;\r\n        case CH_TYPE_J: max=12000; break;\r\n        case CH_TYPE_PT100: max=4000; break;\r\n        default: return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        }\r\n        if((i>=40)!=(c->type==CH_TYPE_PT100)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        if(c->band_C<2 || c->band_C>50 || c->alarm_dC<0 || c->alarm_dC>=c->trip_dC ||\r\n           c->trip_dC>c->probe_limit_dC || c->probe_limit_dC>max) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        ++fitted;\r\n    }\r\n    return fitted?RES_OK:RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n}\r\nres_t set_pack(const settings_t *s, uint8_t out[SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE])\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i; uint16_t end;\r\n    if(out==NULL || set_validate(s)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    memset(out,0,SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE);\r\n    put16(out,0x5354); out[2]=1; out[3]=s->board_type; out[4]=s->channel_count;\r\n    put32(out+6,s->sequence); out[10]=s->address; out[11]=s->baud; put16(out+12,s->pin_bcd);\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) {\r\n        const chan_cfg_t *c=&s->ch[i]; uint8_t *p=out+16u+16u*i;\r\n        p[0]=(uint8_t)c->type; p[1]=(uint8_t)c->mode; memcpy(p+2,c->name,6);\r\n        put16(p+8,(uint16_t)c->alarm_dC); put16(p+10,(uint16_t)c->trip_dC);\r\n        p[12]=c->band_C; p[13]=c->type_epoch; put16(p+14,(uint16_t)c->probe_limit_dC);\r\n    }\r\n    end=(uint16_t)(16u+16u*s->channel_count); put16(out+end,set_crc16(out,end));\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nres_t set_unpack(const uint8_t in[SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE], uint8_t board_type,\r\n                 uint8_t channel_count, settings_t *s)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i; uint16_t end;\r\n    if(in==NULL || s==NULL || channel_count>MAX_CHANNELS) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    memset(s,0,sizeof(*s));\r\n    if(get16(in)!=0x5354 || in[2]!=1 || in[3]!=board_type || in[4]!=channel_count ||\r\n       in[5]!=0 || in[14]!=0 || in[15]!=0) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    end=(uint16_t)(16u+16u*channel_count);\r\n    if(get16(in+end)!=set_crc16(in,end)) return RES_ERR_CRC;\r\n    s->board_type=in[3]; s->channel_count=in[4]; s->sequence=get32(in+6);\r\n    s->address=in[10]; s->baud=in[11]; s->pin_bcd=get16(in+12);\r\n    for(i=0;i<channel_count;++i) {\r\n        chan_cfg_t *c=&s->ch[i]; const uint8_t *p=in+16u+16u*i;\r\n        c->type=(ch_type_t)p[0]; c->mode=(ch_mode_t)p[1]; memcpy(c->name,p+2,6);\r\n        c->alarm_dC=geti16(p+8); c->trip_dC=geti16(p+10); c->band_C=p[12];\r\n        c->type_epoch=p[13]; c->probe_limit_dC=geti16(p+14);\r\n    }\r\n    return set_validate(s);\r\n}\r\nint set_select(bool av, uint32_t a, bool bv, uint32_t b)\r\n{\r\n    uint32_t d=b-a;\r\n    if(!av) return bv?1:-1;\r\n    if(!bv) return 0;\r\n    return (d!=0 && d<UINT32_C(0x80000000))?1:0;\r\n}\r\nbool set_protection_changed(const settings_t *a, const settings_t *b)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(a==NULL || b==NULL || a->board_type!=b->board_type || a->channel_count!=b->channel_count ||\r\n       a->channel_count>MAX_CHANNELS) return true;\r\n    for(i=0;i<a->channel_count;++i) {\r\n        const chan_cfg_t *x=&a->ch[i], *y=&b->ch[i];\r\n        if(x->type!=y->type || x->mode!=y->mode || x->alarm_dC!=y->alarm_dC ||\r\n           x->trip_dC!=y->trip_dC || x->band_C!=y->band_C ||\r\n           x->probe_limit_dC!=y->probe_limit_dC || x->type_epoch!=y->type_epoch) return true;\r\n    }\r\n    return false;\r\n}\r\nres_t set_change_type(chan_cfg_t *c, ch_type_t type)\r\n{\r\n    if(c==NULL || (unsigned)type>CH_TYPE_PT100 || c->type_epoch>63) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(type==c->type) return RES_OK;\r\n    c->type=type; c->type_epoch=(uint8_t)((c->type_epoch+1u)&63u);\r\n    c->alarm_dC=0; c->trip_dC=0; c->probe_limit_dC=0;\r\n    if(type==CH_TYPE_OFF) { c->mode=CH_MODE_TRIP; c->band_C=2; }\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\n#include \"services/settings.h\"\r\n#include \"settings_bytes.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\nres_t cal_validate(const calibration_t *c)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(c==NULL || c->bank_count<1 || c->bank_count>MAX_BANKS) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_BANKS;++i) {\r\n        if(i>=c->bank_count) { if(c->ref_ppm[i]!=0) return RES_ERR_RANGE; }\r\n        else if(c->ref_ppm[i]!=CAL_MISSING && (c->ref_ppm[i]<-10000 || c->ref_ppm[i]>10000)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    }\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_CHANNELS;++i) {\r\n        if(c->baseline_nV[i]==CAL_MISSING) { if(c->tag[i]!=0) return RES_ERR_RANGE; }\r\n        else if(c->baseline_nV[i]<1500000 || c->baseline_nV[i]>10000000 ||\r\n                ((c->tag[i]&3u)!=1u && (c->tag[i]&3u)!=2u)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    }\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_pack(const calibration_t *c, uint8_t out[CAL_SLOT_SIZE])\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(out==NULL || cal_validate(c)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    memset(out,0,CAL_SLOT_SIZE); put16(out,0x434C); out[2]=1; out[3]=c->bank_count;\r\n    put32(out+4,c->sequence);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_BANKS;++i) put32(out+8u+4u*i,(uint32_t)c->ref_ppm[i]);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_CHANNELS;++i) {\r\n        put32(out+32u+4u*i,(uint32_t)c->baseline_nV[i]); out[204u+i]=c->tag[i];\r\n    }\r\n    put16(out+247,set_crc16(out,247)); return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_unpack(const uint8_t in[CAL_SLOT_SIZE], uint8_t banks, calibration_t *c)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(in==NULL || c==NULL) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    memset(c,0,sizeof(*c));\r\n    if(get16(in)!=0x434C || in[2]!=1 || in[3]!=banks) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(get16(in+247)!=set_crc16(in,247)) return RES_ERR_CRC;\r\n    c->bank_count=banks; c->sequence=get32(in+4);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_BANKS;++i) c->ref_ppm[i]=geti32(in+8u+4u*i);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_CHANNELS;++i) { c->baseline_nV[i]=geti32(in+32u+4u*i); c->tag[i]=in[204u+i]; }\r\n    return cal_validate(c);\r\n}\r\nbool cal_complete(const calibration_t *c, const settings_t *s)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i, banks;\r\n    if(cal_validate(c)!=RES_OK || set_validate(s)!=RES_OK) return false;\r\n    banks=s->board_type==40?6u:(uint8_t)(s->channel_count/8u);\r\n    if(c->bank_count!=banks) return false;\r\n    for(i=0;i<banks;++i) if(c->ref_ppm[i]==CAL_MISSING) return false;\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) if(s->ch[i].type!=CH_TYPE_OFF) {\r\n        /* PT100 calibration/tag format is not specified; fail closed until F0-40. */\r\n        if(s->ch[i].type==CH_TYPE_PT100 || c->baseline_nV[i]==CAL_MISSING ||\r\n           c->tag[i]!=(uint8_t)((s->ch[i].type_epoch<<2)|(uint8_t)s->ch[i].type)) return false;\r\n    }\r\n    return true;\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_learn(calibration_t *c, const settings_t *s, const int32_t baseline_nV[MAX_CHANNELS])\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(cal_validate(c)!=RES_OK || set_validate(s)!=RES_OK || baseline_nV==NULL) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) if(s->ch[i].type!=CH_TYPE_OFF &&\r\n        (s->ch[i].type==CH_TYPE_PT100 || baseline_nV[i]<1500000 || baseline_nV[i]>10000000)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) if(s->ch[i].type!=CH_TYPE_OFF) {\r\n        c->baseline_nV[i]=baseline_nV[i];\r\n        c->tag[i]=(uint8_t)((s->ch[i].type_epoch<<2)|(uint8_t)s->ch[i].type);\r\n    }\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/scan.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/drivers/tmp126.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/drivers/keys.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/mcal/timer.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/board/board_cfg_24.c; Get-Content firmware/family/include/board/board_cfg.h; Get-Content firmware/family/test/integration/avr_profile.c; Get-Content firmware/family/test/integration/profile_summary.py'","aggregated_output":"#include \"services/scan.h\"\r\n#include \"app/acquisition_budget.h\"\r\n#include \"services/tc_math.h\"\r\n#include \"drivers/ad7124.h\"\r\n#include \"drivers/tmp126.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/gpio.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/timer.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/wdt.h\"\r\n#include \"board/board_cfg.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\ntypedef enum { INIT_ADC, INIT_CJ, WAIT_CJ, REF_PRE, REF_HIGH, REF_LOW,\r\n               BEGIN_SCAN, READ_CJ, START_SLOT, POLL_SLOT, END_SCAN, RECOVER } phase_t;\r\nstatic phase_t phase;\r\nstatic scan_out_t work,published;\r\nstatic scan_diag_t diag;\r\nstatic const settings_t *cfg;\r\nstatic const calibration_t *cal;\r\nstatic fault_registry_t *registry;\r\nstatic uint32_t start,progress,wait_start,pending,last_ref;\r\nstatic uint8_t initialized,slot,done,cj_index,end_index;\r\nstatic bool prior[MAX_BANKS],good[MAX_BANKS],verify_done[MAX_BANKS],reinit,transport[MAX_BANKS];\r\nstatic int32_t cj_mC[10];\r\nstatic bool cj_valid[10];\r\nstatic uint16_t cm_bad[MAX_BANKS];\r\nstatic void raise(fault_code_t f,uint8_t u) { if(registry && f!=FC_NONE) (void)fault_raise(registry,f,u); }\r\nstatic void bank_fault(uint8_t b,fault_code_t f) {\r\n    if(f==FC_NONE) f=FC_B05_ADC_STALLED;\r\n    good[b]=false; if(f!=FC_B06_REF) diag.cal_safe[b]=false; raise(f,b);\r\n}\r\nemf_nV_t scan_emf(uint32_t code,uint8_t gain) {\r\n    int64_t d=(int32_t)code-0x800000L;\r\n    /* Symmetric nearest rounding; avoids implementation-dependent negative shifts. */\r\n    int64_t n=d*2500000000LL,div=(int64_t)gain*8388608L;\r\n    n=n>=0?(n+div/2)/div:-((-n+div/2)/div);\r\n    if(n>INT32_MAX) return INT32_MAX;\r\n    if(n<INT32_MIN) return INT32_MIN;\r\n    return (emf_nV_t)n;\r\n}\r\nfault_code_t scan_limit(uint8_t s,uint32_t code,uint32_t partner,int32_t ref,\r\n                       int32_t baseline,uint32_t tc) {\r\n    int32_t d=(int32_t)code-0x800000L,v=scan_emf(code,s==11 || s==12?1:32);\r\n    int32_t other; int64_t diff;\r\n    switch(s) {\r\n    case 8: { /* OPEN-Q9: +/-1.6% from production ratio */\r\n        int64_t nominal=6990507LL*(1000000LL+ref)/1000000LL;\r\n        if(ref==CAL_MISSING || ref < -10000 || ref>10000 ||\r\n           (int64_t)d*1000<nominal*984 || (int64_t)d*1000>nominal*1016) return FC_B06_REF;\r\n        break;\r\n    }\r\n    case 9: if(v < -50000 || v>50000) return FC_B08_ZERO; break;\r\n    case 10: if(v<15000000 || v>25000000) return FC_B09_GAIN; break;\r\n    case 11:\r\n        other=scan_emf(partner,32); diff=(int64_t)other-v;\r\n        if(v<=0 || (int64_t)diff*1000 < -(int64_t)v*5 || (int64_t)diff*1000>(int64_t)v*5) return FC_B09_GAIN;\r\n        break;\r\n    case 12: /* AVDD=6*V; compare without overflowing int32. */\r\n        if((int64_t)v*6<3150000000LL || (int64_t)v*6>3450000000LL) return FC_B07_AVDD;\r\n        break;\r\n    case 13: if(d*20LL<8388608LL || d*20LL>19LL*8388608LL) return FC_C03_COMMON_MODE; break;\r\n    case 14:\r\n        if(d>=7549748L) return FC_C01_OPEN;\r\n        if(baseline==CAL_MISSING) return FC_G10_CALIBRATION; /* OPEN-Q10: lock, never invent baseline */\r\n        diff=v-scan_emf(tc,32);\r\n        if((int64_t)diff>2LL*baseline) return FC_C01_OPEN;\r\n        if(2LL*diff<baseline) return FC_C06_SHORTED;\r\n        break;\r\n    default: if(d<=-8220836L || d>=8220836L) return FC_C02_RANGE; break;\r\n    }\r\n    return FC_NONE; /* All diagnostic windows provisional: 03 section 4. */\r\n}\r\nvoid scan_restart(void) {\r\n    phase=INIT_ADC; initialized=0; cj_index=0; reinit=false; diag.initialized=false;\r\n    diag.ref_test_ok=false; wait_start=tick_ms(); ad_reset_state(); cj_reset();\r\n    memset(prior,0,sizeof prior); gpio_write(board()->reftest,false);\r\n}\r\nvoid scan_init(const settings_t *s,const calibration_t *c,fault_registry_t *r) {\r\n    cfg=s; cal=c; registry=r; memset(&published,0,sizeof published); memset(&work,0,sizeof work);\r\n    memset(cm_bad,0,sizeof cm_bad);\r\n    memset(&diag,0,sizeof diag); pending=0; progress=tick_ms(); last_ref=tick_ms(); scan_restart();\r\n}\r\nstatic void publish(void) {\r\n    uint8_t b,c; bool all=true,all_transport=true,all_fault=true;\r\n    work.scan_validated=true;\r\n    for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) {\r\n        work.bank[b]=good[b]?BANK_VALIDATED:BANK_FAULT; all&=good[b]; all_transport&=transport[b]; all_fault&=!good[b];\r\n        prior[b]=good[b];\r\n    }\r\n    if(all_transport || (gpio_read(board()->refok) && all_fault)) { raise(FC_G14_ISLAND_LOST,0); reinit=true; }\r\n    if(gpio_read(board()->refok)) { raise(FC_G08_ENGREF_LOST,0); all=false; }\r\n    diag.duration_ms=(uint16_t)(tick_ms()-start);\r\n    if(tick_ms()-start>1000) { raise(FC_G05_SCAN_DEADLINE,0); all=false; }\r\n    if(!fuses_ok()) { raise(FC_G15_FUSES,0); all=false; }\r\n    if(registry && fault_active(registry,FC_G15_FUSES)) all=false;\r\n    work.scan_validated=all && diag.ref_test_ok && !reinit;\r\n    for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) diag.cal_safe[b]&=diag.registers_ok[b] && !reinit;\r\n    work.completed_ms=tick_ms();\r\n    /* Bad bank diagnostics revoke current validity; channel failures do not invalidate its bank. */\r\n    for(c=0;c<board()->channels;c++) if(!good[board()->channel[c].bank]) work.meas[c].flags&=0xFE;\r\n    published=work;\r\n    if(work.scan_validated && registry) {\r\n        fault_clear(registry,FC_G05_SCAN_DEADLINE,0); fault_clear(registry,FC_G08_ENGREF_LOST,0);\r\n        fault_clear(registry,FC_G14_ISLAND_LOST,0);\r\n    }\r\n    phase=reinit?RECOVER:BEGIN_SCAN; wait_start=tick_ms(); progress=tick_ms();\r\n}\r\nstatic void channel_fault(uint8_t ch,fault_code_t f) {\r\n    uint8_t flag=0;\r\n    switch(f) {\r\n    case FC_C01_OPEN:flag=MEAS_OPEN;break; case FC_C02_RANGE:flag=MEAS_RANGE;break;\r\n    case FC_C03_COMMON_MODE:flag=MEAS_CM_FAIL;break; case FC_C06_SHORTED:flag=MEAS_SHORTED;break;\r\n    case FC_C07_OVUV:flag=MEAS_OVUV;break; case FC_C08_COLD:flag=MEAS_COLD;break;\r\n    default:break;\r\n    }\r\n    work.meas[ch].flags=(uint8_t)((work.meas[ch].flags&~MEAS_VALID)|flag);\r\n    if(f!=FC_C03_COMMON_MODE) raise(f,ch); /* C03 registry unit is the physical input pin. */\r\n}\r\nstatic void result(uint8_t b,uint32_t code) {\r\n    uint8_t ch=(uint8_t)(8*b+slot),target=(uint8_t)(8*b+work.scan_no%8);\r\n    fault_code_t f=ad_fault(b),limit; int32_t base=CAL_MISSING,ref=CAL_MISSING;\r\n    diag.raw[b][slot]=code;\r\n    if(slot==8 && f!=FC_NONE) diag.cal_safe[b]=false;\r\n    if(cal) { ref=cal->ref_ppm[b];\r\n        if(cfg && cal->tag[target]==(uint8_t)((cfg->ch[target].type_epoch<<2)|cfg->ch[target].type)) base=cal->baseline_nV[target];\r\n    }\r\n    if(f>=FC_B01_ADC_ID && f<=FC_B15_ADC_RESET) bank_fault(b,f);\r\n    else if(f!=FC_NONE) channel_fault(slot<8?ch:slot==13?(uint8_t)(8*b+(work.scan_no%16)/2):target,f);\r\n    limit=scan_limit(slot,code,diag.raw[b][10],ref,base,diag.raw[b][work.scan_no%8]);\r\n    if(limit>=FC_B01_ADC_ID && limit<=FC_B15_ADC_RESET) bank_fault(b,limit);\r\n    /* OFF has no learned baseline/tag (05 Â§6). Its burnout result cannot\r\n     * lock a partially fitted board; REF calibration remains mandatory. */\r\n    if(slot==14 && cfg && cfg->ch[target].type==CH_TYPE_OFF) limit=FC_NONE;\r\n    if(limit==FC_G10_CALIBRATION) raise(limit,0);\r\n    if(slot<8) {\r\n        result_t *m=&work.meas[ch];\r\n        m->scan_no=work.scan_no; m->emf_nV=scan_emf(code,32); m->temp_dC=TEMP_DC_INVALID;\r\n        /* Advisory CM/burn flags persist until their next scheduled check. */\r\n        m->flags&=(MEAS_CM_FAIL|MEAS_OPEN|MEAS_SHORTED);\r\n        if(limit!=FC_NONE) channel_fault(ch,limit);\r\n        else if(f!=FC_NONE) channel_fault(ch,f);\r\n        else if(good[b] && cj_valid[2*b] && cj_valid[2*b+1]) {\r\n            uint16_t w=board()->channel[ch].cj_weight_q8;\r\n            int32_t cj=cj_mC[2*b]+(int32_t)(((int64_t)(cj_mC[2*b+1]-cj_mC[2*b])*w)/256);\r\n            ch_type_t type=cfg?cfg->ch[ch].type:CH_TYPE_K;\r\n            uint8_t flags=tc_convert(type,m->emf_nV,(temp_dC_t)(cj/100),&m->temp_dC);\r\n            m->flags|=(uint8_t)(flags&~MEAS_VALID);\r\n            if(prior[b] && (flags&MEAS_VALID) && !(m->flags&~MEAS_VALID)) m->flags|=MEAS_VALID;\r\n            if(flags&MEAS_COLD) raise(FC_C08_COLD,ch);\r\n            if(flags&MEAS_RANGE) raise(FC_C02_RANGE,ch);\r\n            if(registry && !(flags&MEAS_RANGE)) fault_clear(registry,FC_C02_RANGE,ch);\r\n            if(registry && !(flags&MEAS_COLD)) fault_clear(registry,FC_C08_COLD,ch);\r\n            if(registry) fault_clear(registry,FC_C07_OVUV,ch);\r\n        }\r\n        pending|=1UL<<ch;\r\n    } else if(slot==13) {\r\n        uint8_t input=(uint8_t)(work.scan_no%16);\r\n        uint16_t bit=(uint16_t)(1u<<input);\r\n        target=(uint8_t)(8*b+(work.scan_no%16)/2);\r\n        if(limit!=FC_NONE || f==FC_C03_COMMON_MODE) { cm_bad[b]|=bit; channel_fault(target,FC_C03_COMMON_MODE); raise(FC_C03_COMMON_MODE,target); }\r\n        else { cm_bad[b]&=(uint16_t)~bit; }\r\n        /* One registry unit per owning channel, retaining both physical pin\r\n         * bits until each clears. Raw pin identity remains in scan_no % 16. */\r\n        if(registry && !(cm_bad[b]&(uint16_t)(3u<<(2*(input/2))))) fault_clear(registry,FC_C03_COMMON_MODE,target);\r\n        if(!(cm_bad[b]&(uint16_t)(3u<<(2*(input/2))))) work.meas[target].flags&=0xF7;\r\n    } else if(slot==14) {\r\n        diag.burnout_nV[target]=scan_emf(code,32)-scan_emf(diag.raw[b][work.scan_no%8],32);\r\n        if(limit==FC_C01_OPEN || limit==FC_C06_SHORTED) channel_fault(target,limit);\r\n        else if(limit==FC_NONE && f==FC_NONE) { work.meas[target].flags&=0xED;\r\n            if(registry) { fault_clear(registry,FC_C01_OPEN,target); fault_clear(registry,FC_C06_SHORTED,target); }\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\nvoid scan_task(void) {\r\n    uint8_t b; res_t r; uint32_t code=0;\r\n    switch(phase) {\r\n    case INIT_ADC:\r\n        for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) if(!(initialized&(1u<<b))) {\r\n            r=ad_init(b);\r\n            if(r==RES_OK) initialized|=(uint8_t)(1u<<b);\r\n            else if(r!=RES_BUSY) { raise(ad_fault(b),b); phase=RECOVER; wait_start=tick_ms(); }\r\n        }\r\n        progress=tick_ms();\r\n        if(initialized==(1u<<board()->banks)-1u) { phase=INIT_CJ; cj_index=0; }\r\n        break;\r\n    case INIT_CJ:\r\n        r=cj_init(cj_index); progress=tick_ms();\r\n        if(r!=RES_OK) { raise(FC_B10_CJ_BOTH,(uint8_t)(cj_index/2)); phase=RECOVER; wait_start=tick_ms(); }\r\n        else if(++cj_index==board()->cj_count) { phase=WAIT_CJ; wait_start=tick_ms(); }\r\n        break;\r\n    case WAIT_CJ: if(tick_ms()-wait_start>=8) { diag.initialized=true; phase=REF_PRE; progress=tick_ms(); } break;\r\n    case REF_PRE:\r\n        if(gpio_read(board()->refok)) { raise(FC_G08_ENGREF_LOST,0); diag.ref_test_ok=false; phase=BEGIN_SCAN; }\r\n        else { gpio_write(board()->reftest,true); phase=REF_HIGH; wait_start=tick_ms(); }\r\n        progress=tick_ms(); break;\r\n    case REF_HIGH:\r\n        if(tick_ms()-wait_start>=5) { /* OPEN-H7: RC-estimated waits, 10 min interval */\r\n            diag.ref_test_ok=gpio_read(board()->refok);\r\n            if(!diag.ref_test_ok) raise(FC_G09_ENGREF_TEST,0);\r\n            gpio_write(board()->reftest,false); phase=REF_LOW; wait_start=tick_ms(); progress=tick_ms();\r\n        } break;\r\n    case REF_LOW:\r\n        if(tick_ms()-wait_start>=20) {\r\n            if(gpio_read(board()->refok)) { raise(FC_G08_ENGREF_LOST,0); diag.ref_test_ok=false; }\r\n            if(diag.ref_test_ok && registry) fault_clear(registry,FC_G09_ENGREF_TEST,0);\r\n            last_ref=tick_ms(); diag.initialized=true; phase=BEGIN_SCAN; progress=tick_ms();\r\n        } break;\r\n    case BEGIN_SCAN:\r\n        if(tick_ms()-last_ref>=600000UL) { phase=REF_PRE; break; }\r\n        start=tick_ms(); ++work.scan_no; work.scan_validated=false; work.settings_seq=cfg?cfg->sequence:0;\r\n        for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) {\r\n            good[b]=true; transport[b]=false; verify_done[b]=false; diag.cal_safe[b]=true; diag.registers_ok[b]=false;\r\n            ad_scan_begin(b,work.scan_no);\r\n            if(ad_fault(b)!=FC_NONE) { bank_fault(b,ad_fault(b)); reinit=true; }\r\n        }\r\n        cj_index=end_index=0; phase=reinit?END_SCAN:READ_CJ; break;\r\n    case READ_CJ:\r\n        r=cj_read(cj_index,&cj_mC[cj_index]); diag.cj_status[cj_index]=r; cj_valid[cj_index]=r==RES_OK; progress=tick_ms();\r\n        if(++cj_index<board()->cj_count) break;\r\n        for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) {\r\n            int32_t diff=cj_mC[2*b]-cj_mC[2*b+1];\r\n            work.cj_dC[b][0]=(temp_dC_t)(cj_mC[2*b]/100); work.cj_dC[b][1]=(temp_dC_t)(cj_mC[2*b+1]/100);\r\n            if(!cj_valid[2*b] && !cj_valid[2*b+1]) bank_fault(b,FC_B10_CJ_BOTH);\r\n            else if(!cj_valid[2*b] || !cj_valid[2*b+1]) bank_fault(b,FC_B12_CJ_ONE);\r\n            else if(diff < -3000 || diff>3000) bank_fault(b,FC_B11_CJ_DIFF); /* OPEN-Q13 */\r\n        }\r\n        slot=0; phase=START_SLOT; break;\r\n    case START_SLOT:\r\n        done=0;\r\n        for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) {\r\n            r=ad_start_slot(b,slot);\r\n            if(r!=RES_OK) { bank_fault(b,ad_fault(b)); transport[b]=r==RES_ERR_CRC || r==RES_ERR_ID; reinit=true; }\r\n        }\r\n        progress=tick_ms(); phase=reinit?END_SCAN:POLL_SLOT; break;\r\n    case POLL_SLOT:\r\n        for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) if(!(done&(1u<<b))) {\r\n            r=ad_poll(b,&code);\r\n            if(r==RES_OK) { result(b,code); done|=(uint8_t)(1u<<b); }\r\n            else if(r!=RES_BUSY) { bank_fault(b,ad_fault(b)); transport[b]=r==RES_ERR_CRC || r==RES_ERR_ID; reinit=true; done|=(uint8_t)(1u<<b); }\r\n            progress=tick_ms();\r\n            if(!verify_done[b] && !reinit) { r=ad_verify(b);\r\n                if(r==RES_OK) verify_done[b]=true;\r\n                else if(r!=RES_BUSY) { bank_fault(b,ad_fault(b)); reinit=true; }\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n        if(reinit) { phase=END_SCAN; break; }\r\n        if(done==(1u<<board()->banks)-1u) { if(++slot==15) phase=END_SCAN; else phase=START_SLOT; }\r\n        break;\r\n    case END_SCAN:\r\n        if(!reinit) for(b=0;b<board()->banks;b++) {\r\n            r=ad_verify_mutable_part(b,end_index); diag.registers_ok[b]=r==RES_OK && verify_done[b];\r\n            if(!diag.registers_ok[b]) {\r\n                bank_fault(b,ad_fault(b)); transport[b]=r==RES_ERR_CRC || r==RES_ERR_ID; reinit=true;\r\n            }\r\n            if(end_index==18 && good[b] && registry) { uint8_t f; for(f=FC_B01_ADC_ID;f<=FC_B15_ADC_RESET;f++) fault_clear(registry,(fault_code_t)f,b); }\r\n        }\r\n        if(!reinit && ++end_index<19) { progress=tick_ms(); break; }\r\n        publish(); break;\r\n    case RECOVER:\r\n        if(tick_ms()-wait_start>=10) { scan_restart(); progress=tick_ms(); }\r\n        break;\r\n    default: raise(FC_G04_INTERNAL,0); scan_restart(); break;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\nconst scan_out_t *scan_last(void) { return &published; }\r\nconst scan_out_t *scan_current(void) { return &work; }\r\nconst scan_diag_t *scan_diagnostics(void) { return &diag; }\r\nuint32_t scan_progress_ms(void) { return progress; }\r\nuint32_t scan_take_results(void) { uint32_t v=pending; pending=0; return v; }\r\n#include \"drivers/tmp126.h\"\r\n#include \"drivers/iso_spi.h\"\r\n#include \"board/board_cfg.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\nstatic uint8_t age[10];\r\nstatic uint16_t last_id[10];\r\nuint16_t cj_crc16(const uint8_t *p,uint8_t n) {\r\n    uint16_t c=0xFFFF; uint8_t i,j;\r\n    for(i=0;i<n;i++) { c^=(uint16_t)p[i]<<8; for(j=0;j<8;j++) c=(uint16_t)((c&0x8000u)?(c<<1)^0x1021u:c<<1); }\r\n    return c;\r\n}\r\nvoid cj_reset(void) { memset(age,0,sizeof age); memset(last_id,0,sizeof last_id); }\r\nuint16_t cj_last_id(uint8_t j) { return j<10?last_id[j]:0; }\r\nstatic uint16_t signature(uint8_t j) { return (uint16_t)(0xC000u+0x40u*j); }\r\nstatic res_t frame(uint8_t j,uint16_t cmd,uint16_t *v) {\r\n    uint8_t bytes[4],k; uint16_t dummy,crc; res_t r;\r\n    if(j>=board()->cj_count) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(k=0;k<2;k++) {\r\n        r=iso_select((uint8_t)(ISO_CJ_BASE+j)); if(r!=RES_OK) return r;\r\n        (void)iso_sio_write_enable(true); (void)iso_word(cmd,&dummy);\r\n        if(cmd&0x100u) {\r\n            (void)iso_sio_write_enable(false); (void)iso_word(0xFFFF,v); (void)iso_word(0xFFFF,&crc);\r\n        } else {\r\n            (void)iso_word(*v,&dummy); crc=0;\r\n            if(cmd&0x4000u) {\r\n                bytes[0]=(uint8_t)(cmd>>8); bytes[1]=(uint8_t)cmd;\r\n                bytes[2]=(uint8_t)(*v>>8); bytes[3]=(uint8_t)*v;\r\n                (void)iso_word(cj_crc16(bytes,4),&dummy);\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n        iso_deselect();\r\n        if(!(cmd&0x100u)) return RES_OK;\r\n        bytes[0]=(uint8_t)(cmd>>8); bytes[1]=(uint8_t)cmd; bytes[2]=(uint8_t)(*v>>8); bytes[3]=(uint8_t)*v;\r\n        if(cj_crc16(bytes,4)==crc) return RES_OK;\r\n    }\r\n    return RES_ERR_CRC;\r\n}\r\nres_t cj_init(uint8_t j) {\r\n    uint16_t v=4; res_t r=frame(j,0x0003,&v); /* OPEN-Q12: configuration write without CRC */\r\n    if(r==RES_OK) r=frame(j,0x4503,&v);\r\n    if(r!=RES_OK) return r; if(v!=4) return RES_ERR_READBACK;\r\n    v=signature(j); r=frame(j,0x4405,&v);\r\n    if(r==RES_OK) r=frame(j,0x4505,&v);\r\n    if(r!=RES_OK) return r;\r\n    age[j]=0; return v==signature(j)?RES_OK:RES_ERR_READBACK;\r\n}\r\nres_t cj_read(uint8_t j,int32_t *t) {\r\n    uint16_t status=0,raw=0,id=0,cfg=0,sig=0; res_t r;\r\n    if(j>=board()->cj_count) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    last_id[j]=0;\r\n    r=frame(j,0x4502,&status); if(r!=RES_OK) return r;\r\n    if(status&0x80u) return RES_ERR_CRC;\r\n    if(status&1u) age[j]=0; else if(age[j]<255) ++age[j];\r\n    r=frame(j,0x4500,&raw); if(r!=RES_OK) return r;\r\n    r=frame(j,0x450C,&id); if(r!=RES_OK) return r;\r\n    last_id[j]=id;\r\n    r=frame(j,0x4503,&cfg); if(r!=RES_OK) return r;\r\n    r=frame(j,0x4505,&sig); if(r!=RES_OK) return r;\r\n    if(id!=0x2126) return RES_ERR_ID;\r\n    if(cfg!=4 || sig!=signature(j)) return RES_ERR_READBACK;\r\n    { int32_t scaled=(int32_t)(int16_t)raw*125;\r\n      *t=scaled>=0?scaled/16:-((-scaled+15)/16); /* exact arithmetic >>4, portable for negatives */\r\n    }\r\n    if(age[j]>2 || *t < -40000 || *t>125000 || (raw&3)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\n#include \"drivers/keys.h\"\r\n#include \"board/board_cfg.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/gpio.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/timer.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\nstatic volatile uint8_t history[5];\r\nstatic volatile uint8_t stable;\r\nstatic uint8_t previous,armed,delivered,pending,press_edges;\r\nstatic uint32_t since[5],repeat_at[2];\r\nstatic bool chord,repeating;\r\nstatic key_event_t queue[8]; static uint8_t head,tail;\r\nstatic void emit(key_t key,uint32_t press,uint32_t now) {\r\n    uint8_t n=(uint8_t)((head+1)&7);\r\n    if(n!=tail) { queue[head].key=key; queue[head].pressed_ms=press; queue[head].event_ms=now; head=n; }\r\n}\r\n/* Gesture rearming must not erase a physical abort edge from this pass. */\r\nvoid keys_rearm(void) { armed=0; pending=0; delivered=0; chord=false; head=tail=0; }\r\nuint8_t keys_pressed(void) { uint8_t p=press_edges; press_edges=0; return p; }\r\nvoid keys_init(void) {\r\n    uint8_t i; for(i=0;i<5;i++) history[i]=0xFF;\r\n    memset(since,0,sizeof since);\r\n    stable=previous=press_edges=0; repeating=false; keys_rearm();\r\n}\r\nvoid keys_sample_isr(void) {\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    for(i=0;i<board()->key_count;i++) {\r\n        history[i]=(uint8_t)((history[i]<<1)|(gpio_read(board()->keys[i])?1u:0u));\r\n        if(history[i]==0) stable|=(uint8_t)(1u<<i);\r\n        else if(history[i]==255) stable&=(uint8_t)~(1u<<i);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\nuint8_t keys_held(void) { return stable; }\r\nvoid keys_repeat(bool e) { repeating=e; }\r\nvoid keys_task(void) {\r\n    uint8_t s=stable,i; uint32_t now=tick_ms();\r\n    press_edges=(uint8_t)(s&~previous);\r\n    for(i=0;i<board()->key_count;i++) {\r\n        uint8_t bit=(uint8_t)(1u<<i);\r\n        if(!(s&bit) && !(previous&bit) && history[i]==255) armed|=bit;\r\n        if((s&bit) && !(previous&bit)) {\r\n            since[i]=now; delivered&=(uint8_t)~bit;\r\n            if((armed&bit) && i<2) { pending|=bit; repeat_at[i]=now+600; }\r\n        }\r\n        if((s&bit) && now-since[i]>30000) { armed&=(uint8_t)~bit; pending&=(uint8_t)~bit; }\r\n    }\r\n    if((s&3)==3 && (pending&3)!=0 && (armed&3)==3 &&\r\n       ((since[0]>since[1]?since[0]-since[1]:since[1]-since[0])<=150)) {\r\n        chord=true; pending&=0xFC;\r\n    }\r\n    for(i=0;i<board()->key_count;i++) {\r\n        uint8_t bit=(uint8_t)(1u<<i); uint32_t held=now-since[i];\r\n        if(!(armed&bit)) continue;\r\n        if((s&bit) && i==3 && held>=50 && !(delivered&bit)) { emit(KEY_ACK,since[i],now); delivered|=bit; }\r\n        if(i<2 && !chord) {\r\n            if((pending&bit) && (held>=150 || !(s&bit))) {\r\n                emit(i==0?KEY_UP:KEY_DOWN,since[i],now); pending&=(uint8_t)~bit; delivered|=bit;\r\n            }\r\n            if(repeating && (s&bit) && (int32_t)(now-repeat_at[i])>=0) {\r\n                emit(i==0?KEY_UP:KEY_DOWN,since[i],now); repeat_at[i]=now+(held>=3000?50u:150u);\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n        if(!(s&bit) && (previous&bit)) {\r\n            if(i==2) emit(held>=3000?KEY_SET_LONG:KEY_SET,since[i],now);\r\n            if(i==4) emit(KEY_ESC,since[i],now);\r\n            armed&=(uint8_t)~bit;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    if(chord && !(s&3)) { emit(KEY_ESC,since[0],now); chord=false; }\r\n    previous=s;\r\n}\r\nbool keys_get_event(key_event_t *event) {\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    for(i=0;i<7 && tail!=head;i++) {\r\n        key_event_t e=queue[tail]; tail=(uint8_t)((tail+1)&7);\r\n        if(e.key!=KEY_ACK || tick_ms()-e.event_ms<=500) { *event=e; return true; }\r\n    }\r\n    return false;\r\n}\r\nkey_t keys_get(void) { key_event_t e; return keys_get_event(&e)?e.key:KEY_NONE; }\r\n#include \"mcal/timer.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/gpio.h\"\r\n#include \"drivers/keys.h\"\r\n#include <avr/io.h>\r\n#include <avr/interrupt.h>\r\n#include <util/atomic.h>\r\nstatic volatile uint32_t ms;\r\nstatic volatile uint16_t deadline;\r\nstatic volatile bool expired;\r\nvoid timer_init(void) {\r\n    ms=0; deadline=0; expired=false; TCCR0A=0; TCCR0B=0; TIMSK0=0;\r\n    TCCR1A=0; TCCR1B=2; TIMSK1=0;\r\n    ASSR=0; TCCR2A=2; TCCR2B=4; OCR2A=124; TIMSK2=2;\r\n}\r\nuint32_t tick_ms(void) { uint32_t v; ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) { v=ms; } return v; }\r\nvoid timer_run_stop(void) {\r\n    ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) { TCCR0A=0; PORTB&=0xF7u; TCCR0B=0; deadline=0; }\r\n}\r\nbool timer_run_start_at(uint16_t d,uint32_t evaluated) {\r\n    bool started=false;\r\n    ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) {\r\n        uint32_t age=ms-evaluated;\r\n        if(d && d<=1000 && age>=d) expired=true;\r\n        if(!expired && d && d<=1000 && age<d) {\r\n            deadline=(uint16_t)(d-age); TCNT0=0; OCR0A=249; TCCR0A=0x42; TCCR0B=2; started=true;\r\n        } else timer_run_stop();\r\n    }\r\n    return started;\r\n}\r\nvoid timer_run_start(uint16_t d) { (void)timer_run_start_at(d,tick_ms()); }\r\nbool timer_run_expired(void) { return expired; }\r\nvoid timer_run_ack_expiry(void) { ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) { if(!deadline && !TCCR0B) expired=false; } }\r\nuint16_t timer_run_remaining(void) { uint16_t v; ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) { v=deadline; } return v; }\r\nbool timer_run_active(void) { return timer_run_remaining()!=0 && TCCR0B!=0; }\r\nvoid timer_run_static_high(void) { timer_run_stop(); ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) { if(!expired) { PORTB|=8; deadline=1000; } } }\r\nvoid timer_tick_isr(void) { ++ms; if(deadline && --deadline==0) { expired=true; timer_run_stop(); } keys_sample_isr(); }\r\nISR(TIMER2_COMPA_vect) { timer_tick_isr(); }\r\n#include \"board/board_cfg.h\"\r\n#define CH(b,k,w) {b,2u*(k),2u*(k)+1u,w}\r\n#define BANK(b) CH(b,0,0),CH(b,1,0),CH(b,2,32),CH(b,3,96),CH(b,4,160),CH(b,5,224),CH(b,6,256),CH(b,7,256)\r\nstatic const board_t cfg = {\r\n    24,3,6,CS_DIRECT,\r\n    {PIN(PORT_B,4),PIN(PORT_B,0),PIN(PORT_B,1),0,0,0},\r\n    {PIN(PORT_B,2),PIN(PORT_C,0),PIN(PORT_C,1),PIN(PORT_C,3),PIN(PORT_C,4),PIN(PORT_C,5),0,0,0,0},\r\n    PIN(PORT_D,5),PIN(PORT_A,2),PIN(PORT_A,3),\r\n    PIN(PORT_B,3),PIN(PORT_C,2),PIN(PORT_C,6),PIN(PORT_C,7),PIN(PORT_D,7),\r\n    {PIN(PORT_D,2),PIN(PORT_D,3),PIN(PORT_D,4),PIN(PORT_D,6),0},4,false,\r\n    {BANK(0),BANK(1),BANK(2)}, /* OPEN-Q14: provisional clamped header weights */\r\n    {0,0x97,0x3B,0x74},{0xFB,0xBF,0x7B,0xA2}\r\n};\r\nconst board_t *board(void) { return &cfg; }\r\n#ifndef FAMILY_BOARD_CFG_H\r\n#define FAMILY_BOARD_CFG_H\r\n#include \"common/types.h\"\r\n/* Encoded port A..D in bits 4:3, bit number in bits 2:0. */\r\ntypedef uint8_t pin_t;\r\n#define PIN(p,b) ((pin_t)((p)*8u+(b)))\r\nenum { PORT_A, PORT_B, PORT_C, PORT_D };\r\ntypedef struct { uint8_t bank, ain_p, ain_m; uint16_t cj_weight_q8; } channel_hw_t;\r\ntypedef enum { CS_DIRECT, CS_DECODER } cs_method_t;\r\ntypedef struct {\r\n    uint8_t channels, banks, cj_count;\r\n    cs_method_t cs_method;\r\n    pin_t adc_cs[6], cj_cs[10], sio_wr_n, refok, reftest;\r\n    pin_t run, run_sense, alarm, alarm_sense, de;\r\n    pin_t keys[5]; uint8_t key_count;\r\n    bool has_rtd;\r\n    channel_hw_t channel[MAX_CHANNELS];\r\n    uint8_t port_init[4],ddr_init[4];\r\n} board_t;\r\n/* Immutable hardware mapping, no settings or temperatures. */\r\nconst board_t *board(void);\r\n#endif\r\n/* AVR instruction simulator harness: real shell and drivers, register fakes.\r\n * No WDR instruction: the GNU simulator does not implement it. */\r\n#include \"app/app.h\"\r\n#include \"app/ee_owner.h\"\r\n#include \"app/service.h\"\r\n#include \"services/scan.h\"\r\n#include \"drivers/keys.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/timer.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/flash_crc.h\"\r\n#include \"fake_hw.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\nvolatile uint16_t profile_pass;\r\nvolatile uint8_t profile_phase;\r\nvolatile uint32_t profile_delay;\r\nuint8_t profile_eeprom_read(uint16_t a) {\r\n    if(a>=0x40 && a<0x640) return fake_eeprom[(a-0x40)%768];\r\n    if(a>=0x640 && a<0x840) return fake_eeprom[768+(a-0x640)%256];\r\n    return 0xFF;\r\n}\r\nvoid profile_eeprom_write(uint16_t a,uint8_t v) {\r\n    if(a>=0x40 && a<0x640) fake_eeprom[(a-0x40)%768]=v;\r\n    if(a>=0x640 && a<0x840) fake_eeprom[768+(a-0x640)%256]=v;\r\n}\r\nvoid flash_crc_begin(void) { }\r\nres_t flash_crc(void) { return RES_OK; }\r\nuint16_t flash_crc_value(void) { return 0; }\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void profile_begin(void) { __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void profile_end(void) { __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void profile_done(void) { for(;;) __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\nstatic void passes(uint16_t n) {\r\n    for(profile_pass=0;profile_pass<n;profile_pass++) {\r\n        bool measure=(profile_phase==2 && profile_pass<750) || (profile_phase==3 && profile_pass==0) ||\r\n            ((profile_phase==4 || profile_phase==5 || profile_phase==8) && profile_pass<20) ||\r\n            (profile_phase==0 && profile_pass==430) || (profile_phase==1 && profile_pass==58) ||\r\n            (profile_phase==6 && profile_pass==652);\r\n        fake_spi_bytes=fake_soft_bytes=profile_delay=0;\r\n        if(measure) profile_begin();\r\n        f0_task();\r\n        if(measure) profile_end();\r\n        fake_advance(1); keys_sample_isr();\r\n    }\r\n}\r\nstatic settings_t cfg;\r\nstatic calibration_t cal;\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) static void fixture(void) {\r\n    uint8_t ch,j;\r\n    fake_reset(); memset(&cfg,0,sizeof cfg); memset(&cal,0,sizeof cal);\r\n    cfg.board_type=cfg.channel_count=24; cfg.address=1; cfg.sequence=7; cal.bank_count=3;\r\n    for(ch=0;ch<MAX_CHANNELS;ch++) {\r\n        for(j=0;j<6;j++) cfg.ch[ch].name[j]=' ';\r\n        cfg.ch[ch].band_C=2; cal.baseline_nV[ch]=CAL_MISSING;\r\n        if(ch<24) {\r\n            cfg.ch[ch].type=CH_TYPE_K; cfg.ch[ch].alarm_dC=800; cfg.ch[ch].trip_dC=1000;\r\n            cfg.ch[ch].probe_limit_dC=12000; cal.baseline_nV[ch]=3200000; cal.tag[ch]=1;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    (void)set_pack(&cfg,fake_eeprom); (void)cal_pack(&cal,fake_eeprom+768);\r\n}\r\nint main(void) {\r\n    uint8_t ch; uint16_t wait;\r\n    fixture();\r\n    f0_init(); profile_phase=0; passes(3100);\r\n    fake_pin(board()->keys[3],false); profile_phase=1; passes(70);\r\n    fake_pin(board()->keys[3],true); profile_phase=2; passes(1500);\r\n    /* Full channel fault fan-out in one pass, followed by durable queue writes. */\r\n    for(ch=0;ch<24;ch++) (void)fault_raise((fault_registry_t *)app_faults(),FC_C01_OPEN,ch);\r\n    profile_phase=3; passes(1800);\r\n    /* Names-only and protection commit command paths. */\r\n    cfg=*app_settings(); cfg.ch[0].name[0]='X'; (void)app_commit_settings(&cfg);\r\n    profile_phase=4; passes(1800);\r\n    cfg=*app_settings(); cfg.ch[0].trip_dC=1100; (void)app_commit_settings(&cfg);\r\n    profile_phase=5; passes(1800);\r\n    /* Service passive, prompts and EEPROM scratch include formatted output. */\r\n    fake_reset(); (void)set_pack(&cfg,fake_eeprom); (void)cal_pack(&cal,fake_eeprom+768);\r\n    fake_pin(board()->keys[2],false); f0_init(); profile_phase=6; passes(12000);\r\n    fake_pin(board()->keys[2],true); passes(220);\r\n    /* Exercise the most expensive pure commit: calibration invalidation on\r\n     * type-epoch wrap, coincident with a full CJ transaction in the loop. */\r\n    fixture(); cfg.ch[0].type_epoch=63; cal.tag[0]=253;\r\n    (void)set_pack(&cfg,fake_eeprom); (void)cal_pack(&cal,fake_eeprom+768);\r\n    f0_init(); profile_phase=7; passes(3000);\r\n    for(wait=0;wait<1600;wait++) { passes(1); if(fake_soft_bytes==30) break; }\r\n    cfg=*app_settings(); cfg.ch[0].type_epoch=0; cfg.ch[0].type=CH_TYPE_J;\r\n    (void)app_commit_settings(&cfg); profile_phase=8; passes(20);\r\n    profile_done();\r\n}\r\n\"\"\"Report AVR instruction measurements separately from register-model CPU.\"\"\"\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\nimport re\r\nimport sys\r\n\r\nroot = Path(sys.argv[1])\r\ntext = (root / \"cycles.log\").read_text()\r\nmarker = None\r\nrows = []\r\nstart = fake = io_start = bound = 0\r\ncount = 0\r\n# Conservative -Os MCAL bounds, including call/return margin. Soft SPI is\r\n# calibrated across all 256 TX values in mcal.log (3234 cycles); reserve 3300.\r\ncosts = {1: 400, 2: 100, 3: 100, 4: 60, 6: 30, 7: 30, 8: 110,\r\n         9: 3300, 10: 100, 11: 40, 12: 300, 13: 300, 14: 100,\r\n         15: 40, 16: 60, 17: 20, 18: 80, 19: 100, 20: 10,\r\n         21: 20, 22: 100, 23: 150, 24: 150, 25: 80, 26: 20,\r\n         27: 100, 28: 100, 29: 100, 30: 80, 31: 60}\r\nfor line in text.splitlines():\r\n    match = re.fullmatch(r\"(BEGIN|END|IO_BEGIN|IO_END)(?: (.*))?\", line)\r\n    if match:\r\n        marker = match[1], list(map(int, (match[2] or \"\").split()))\r\n    match = re.match(r\"# cycles\\s+(\\d+)\", line.strip())\r\n    if not match or not marker:\r\n        continue\r\n    kind, values = marker\r\n    marker = None\r\n    cycles = int(match[1])\r\n    if kind == \"BEGIN\":\r\n        start = cycles\r\n        fake = bound = count = 0\r\n    elif kind == \"IO_BEGIN\":\r\n        io_start = cycles\r\n        io, arg = values\r\n        bound += 16 * arg + 40 if io == 5 else costs[io]\r\n        count += 1\r\n    elif kind == \"IO_END\":\r\n        fake += cycles - io_start + 4  # breakpoint precedes the RET\r\n    elif count:\r\n        application = cycles - start - fake\r\n        # 25% + 2048 cycles reserves Timer2 and full-duplex UART interrupts.\r\n        # Measured Timer2 ISR=716 cycles. At 38400 baud, 2*3840 UART ISRs/s,\r\n        # each <=100 cycles: <19% CPU. This is a running-loop estimate, not\r\n        # exhaustive WCET; failures/timeouts and input-driven branches remain.\r\n        estimate = ((application + bound) * 5 + 3) // 4 + 2048\r\n        rows.append((estimate, application, bound, *values[:2]))\r\nassert rows and \"profile_done\" in text, \"Incomplete simulator run\"\r\nworst = max(rows)\r\nsummary = [\"cycles,production_cpu,mcal_bound,phase,pass\"]\r\nsummary += [\",\".join(map(str, row)) for row in rows]\r\n(root / \"passes.csv\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(summary) + \"\\n\")\r\nprint(f\"AVR running-loop estimate: {worst[0]} cycles / {worst[0]/8000:.3f} ms \"\r\n      f\"(phase {worst[3]}, pass {worst[4]}); 64000-cycle budget EXCEEDED\")\r\nprint(f\"Components: production={worst[1]}, MCAL bound={worst[2]}, \"\r\n      \"interrupt reserve=25% + 2048 cycles\")\r\ncommit = (root / \"commit.log\").read_text()\r\nticks = list(map(int, re.findall(r\"# cycles\\s+(\\d+)\", commit)))\r\nassert len(ticks) == 2, \"Incomplete pure commit measurement\"\r\nassert \"RES_OK\" in commit, \"Pure commit did not start\"\r\nprint(f\"set_commit_with_cal alone: {ticks[1]-ticks[0]} cycles / \"\r\n      f\"{(ticks[1]-ticks[0])/8000:.4f} ms\")\r\nwrap = (root / \"wrap.log\").read_text()\r\nticks = list(map(int, re.findall(r\"# cycles\\s+(\\d+)\", wrap)))\r\nassert len(ticks) == 2, \"Incomplete epoch-wrap measurement\"\r\nassert \"RES_OK\" in wrap, \"Epoch-wrap commit did not start\"\r\nprint(f\"Epoch-wrap commit alone: {ticks[1]-ticks[0]} cycles / \"\r\n      f\"{(ticks[1]-ticks[0])/8000:.4f} ms\")\r\nmcal = (root / \"mcal.log\").read_text()\r\ncalibration = {}\r\nfor kind, _, begin, end in re.findall(\r\n        r\"BEGIN (\\d+) (\\d+)\\n.*?# cycles\\s+(\\d+)\\n.*?END\\n.*?# cycles\\s+(\\d+)\",\r\n        mcal, re.S):\r\n    calibration.setdefault(int(kind), []).append(int(end)-int(begin))\r\nassert len(calibration[9]) == 256 and calibration[32], \"Incomplete MCAL calibration\"\r\nprint(f\"Real soft SPI: {max(calibration[9])} cycles/byte; \"\r\n      f\"30-byte CJ transaction={30*max(calibration[9])} cycles; \"\r\n      f\"Timer2 ISR={max(calibration[32])} cycles\")\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"rg --files | rg -i 'tmp126|datasheet|02-hardware'; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_store.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_cal.c; Get-Content firmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c | Select-Object -First 100; rg -n 'st\\\\.image|store\\\\.image|phase==STORE_INVALIDATE|STORE_INVALIDATE|set_commit\\\\(|set_commit_with_cal\\\\(|cal_commit\\\\(' firmware/family/test/acceptance firmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/app/ee_owner.c\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"rg --files | rg -i 'tmp126|datasheet|02-hardware'; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_store.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/services/settings_cal.c; Get-Content firmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c | Select-Object -First 100; rg -n 'st\\\\.image|store\\\\.image|phase==STORE_INVALIDATE|STORE_INVALIDATE|set_commit\\\\(|set_commit_with_cal\\\\(|cal_commit\\\\(' firmware/family/test/acceptance firmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c; Get-Content firmware/family/src/app/ee_owner.c\"","aggregated_output":"docs\\reference\\datasheets\\TSR1-series.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\README.md\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\R-78HB-0.5.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\MAX31856.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\LP2985.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\LM74930.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\LM5164.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\ISO7761.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\ISO7760.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\G5LE-relay.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\BSS131.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\ATmega32A.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\ADM2587E.pdf\r\ndocs\\reference\\datasheets\\1812L-PTC.pdf\r\nfirmware\\spec\\02-hardware-interface.md\r\ndocs\\decisions\\0041-24ch-rev-a4-gated-tmp126-sio-driver.md\r\nfirmware\\family\\test\\fakes\\fake_tmp126.c\r\nfirmware\\family\\src\\drivers\\tmp126.c\r\nfirmware\\family\\include\\drivers\\tmp126.h\r\n#include \"services/settings.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\nvoid set_store_init(set_store_t *st)\r\n{\r\n    if(st!=NULL) { memset(st,0,sizeof(*st)); st->active_slot=2; st->calibration_active_slot=2; }\r\n}\r\nstatic bool available(const set_store_t *st)\r\n{ return st->phase==STORE_IDLE || st->phase==STORE_DONE || st->phase==STORE_FAILED; }\r\nstatic void begin(set_store_t *s, uint8_t active, uint16_t size, bool cal, bool prot)\r\n{\r\n    s->phase=STORE_INVALIDATE; s->active_slot=active;\r\n    s->target_slot=active==0?1:0;\r\n    s->base=(uint16_t)(cal?(0x640u+256u*s->target_slot):(0x40u+768u*s->target_slot));\r\n    s->length=size; s->index=2; s->pending=false; s->retries=0;\r\n    s->calibration=cal; s->protection_change=prot;\r\n    s->settings_after_cal=false;\r\n    if(cal) { s->calibration_active_slot=active; s->calibration_slot_known=true; }\r\n}\r\nstatic res_t settings_commit(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate,\r\n                             const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot,\r\n                             const calibration_t *cal, uint8_t cal_slot)\r\n{\r\n    settings_t next; calibration_t next_cal; uint8_t i; bool wraps=false;\r\n    if(st==NULL || active_slot>2 || set_validate(candidate)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(!available(st)) return RES_BUSY;\r\n    if(active!=NULL) {\r\n        if(active_slot>1 || set_validate(active)!=RES_OK || candidate->board_type!=active->board_type ||\r\n           candidate->channel_count!=active->channel_count) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        /* Epoch changes are enforced at the commit boundary, not trusted to UI. */\r\n        for(i=0;i<active->channel_count;++i) {\r\n            uint8_t expected=active->ch[i].type_epoch;\r\n            if(active->ch[i].type!=candidate->ch[i].type) expected=(uint8_t)((expected+1u)&63u);\r\n            if(candidate->ch[i].type_epoch!=expected) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n            if(active->ch[i].type_epoch==63 && expected==0) wraps=true;\r\n        }\r\n    } else if(active_slot!=2) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(wraps) {\r\n        uint8_t banks=candidate->board_type==40?6u:(uint8_t)(candidate->channel_count/8u);\r\n        if(cal_slot>1 || cal_validate(cal)!=RES_OK || cal->bank_count!=banks) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        /* A settings verification failure may leave its copy boot-selectable.\r\n         * Never overwrite the verified cleared calibration using a stale slot\r\n         * on retry: that would briefly expose the ancient baseline again. */\r\n        if(st->calibration_slot_known && cal_slot!=st->calibration_active_slot) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n        next_cal=*cal; next_cal.sequence=cal->sequence+1u;\r\n        for(i=0;i<active->channel_count;++i)\r\n            if(active->ch[i].type_epoch==63 && candidate->ch[i].type_epoch==0) {\r\n                next_cal.baseline_nV[i]=CAL_MISSING; next_cal.tag[i]=0;\r\n            }\r\n        if(cal_pack(&next_cal,st->wrap_cal_image)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    }\r\n    next=*candidate; next.sequence=active?active->sequence+1u:0;\r\n    if(set_pack(&next,st->image)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    begin(st,active_slot,(uint16_t)(18u+16u*next.channel_count),false,set_protection_changed(active,&next));\r\n    if(wraps) {\r\n        begin(st,cal_slot,249,true,true);\r\n        st->active_slot=active_slot; st->settings_after_cal=true;\r\n    }\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nres_t set_commit(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate, const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot)\r\n{\r\n    return settings_commit(st,candidate,active,active_slot,NULL,2);\r\n}\r\nres_t set_commit_with_cal(set_store_t *st, const settings_t *candidate,\r\n                          const settings_t *active, uint8_t active_slot,\r\n                          const calibration_t *active_cal, uint8_t cal_slot)\r\n{\r\n    return settings_commit(st,candidate,active,active_slot,active_cal,cal_slot);\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_commit(set_store_t *st, const calibration_t *candidate, uint32_t active_sequence, uint8_t active_slot)\r\n{\r\n    calibration_t next;\r\n    if(st==NULL || active_slot>2 || cal_validate(candidate)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(!available(st)) return RES_BUSY;\r\n    if(st->calibration_slot_known && active_slot!=st->calibration_active_slot) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    next=*candidate; next.sequence=active_slot==2?0:active_sequence+1u;\r\n    if(cal_pack(&next,st->image)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    begin(st,active_slot,249,true,true); return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nstatic void retry_or_fail(set_store_t *s)\r\n{\r\n    s->pending=false;\r\n    if(s->fault!=FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT) s->fault=s->protection_change?FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT:FC_G13_SAVE_FAIL_INFO;\r\n    if(s->retries==0) { s->retries=1; s->phase=STORE_INVALIDATE; s->index=2; }\r\n    else s->phase=STORE_FAILED;\r\n}\r\nstatic const uint8_t *store_image(const set_store_t *s)\r\n{ return s->settings_after_cal?s->wrap_cal_image:s->image; }\r\nvoid set_store_step(set_store_t *s, bool ready, bool success, uint8_t value, ee_op_t *op)\r\n{\r\n    if(op==NULL) return;\r\n    memset(op,0,sizeof(*op));\r\n    if(s==NULL || !ready) return;\r\n    if(s->phase==STORE_IDLE || s->phase==STORE_DONE || s->phase==STORE_FAILED) return;\r\n    if(s->pending) {\r\n        s->pending=false;\r\n        if(!success || (s->phase==STORE_VERIFY && value!=store_image(s)[s->index])) retry_or_fail(s);\r\n        else switch(s->phase) {\r\n        case STORE_INVALIDATE: s->phase=STORE_BODY; s->index=2; break;\r\n        case STORE_BODY:\r\n            ++s->index;\r\n            if(s->index==s->length) { s->phase=STORE_MAGIC; s->index=1; }\r\n            break;\r\n        case STORE_MAGIC:\r\n            if(s->index==1) s->index=0;\r\n            else { s->phase=STORE_VERIFY; s->index=0; }\r\n            break;\r\n        case STORE_VERIFY:\r\n            ++s->index;\r\n            if(s->index==s->length) {\r\n                if(s->settings_after_cal) {\r\n                    uint8_t settings_slot=s->active_slot, cal_slot=s->target_slot;\r\n                    begin(s,settings_slot,(uint16_t)(18u+16u*s->image[4]),false,true);\r\n                    s->calibration_active_slot=cal_slot;\r\n                } else {\r\n                    s->phase=STORE_DONE; s->active_slot=s->target_slot;\r\n                    if(s->calibration) s->calibration_active_slot=s->target_slot;\r\n                    if(s->fault!=FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT || s->protection_change) s->fault=FC_NONE;\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n            break;\r\n        default: retry_or_fail(s); break;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    switch(s->phase) {\r\n    case STORE_INVALIDATE: op->kind=EE_WRITE; op->address=s->base; op->value=0; break;\r\n    case STORE_BODY: case STORE_MAGIC:\r\n        op->kind=EE_WRITE; op->address=(uint16_t)(s->base+s->index); op->value=store_image(s)[s->index]; break;\r\n    case STORE_VERIFY: op->kind=EE_READ; op->address=(uint16_t)(s->base+s->index); break;\r\n    case STORE_DONE: case STORE_FAILED: case STORE_IDLE: return;\r\n    default: s->phase=STORE_FAILED; s->fault=FC_G02_SAVE_FAIL_PROT; return;\r\n    }\r\n    s->pending=true;\r\n}\r\n#include \"services/settings.h\"\r\n#include \"settings_bytes.h\"\r\n#include <string.h>\r\nres_t cal_validate(const calibration_t *c)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(c==NULL || c->bank_count<1 || c->bank_count>MAX_BANKS) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_BANKS;++i) {\r\n        if(i>=c->bank_count) { if(c->ref_ppm[i]!=0) return RES_ERR_RANGE; }\r\n        else if(c->ref_ppm[i]!=CAL_MISSING && (c->ref_ppm[i]<-10000 || c->ref_ppm[i]>10000)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    }\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_CHANNELS;++i) {\r\n        if(c->baseline_nV[i]==CAL_MISSING) { if(c->tag[i]!=0) return RES_ERR_RANGE; }\r\n        else if(c->baseline_nV[i]<1500000 || c->baseline_nV[i]>10000000 ||\r\n                ((c->tag[i]&3u)!=1u && (c->tag[i]&3u)!=2u)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    }\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_pack(const calibration_t *c, uint8_t out[CAL_SLOT_SIZE])\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(out==NULL || cal_validate(c)!=RES_OK) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    memset(out,0,CAL_SLOT_SIZE); put16(out,0x434C); out[2]=1; out[3]=c->bank_count;\r\n    put32(out+4,c->sequence);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_BANKS;++i) put32(out+8u+4u*i,(uint32_t)c->ref_ppm[i]);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_CHANNELS;++i) {\r\n        put32(out+32u+4u*i,(uint32_t)c->baseline_nV[i]); out[204u+i]=c->tag[i];\r\n    }\r\n    put16(out+247,set_crc16(out,247)); return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_unpack(const uint8_t in[CAL_SLOT_SIZE], uint8_t banks, calibration_t *c)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(in==NULL || c==NULL) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    memset(c,0,sizeof(*c));\r\n    if(get16(in)!=0x434C || in[2]!=1 || in[3]!=banks) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    if(get16(in+247)!=set_crc16(in,247)) return RES_ERR_CRC;\r\n    c->bank_count=banks; c->sequence=get32(in+4);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_BANKS;++i) c->ref_ppm[i]=geti32(in+8u+4u*i);\r\n    for(i=0;i<MAX_CHANNELS;++i) { c->baseline_nV[i]=geti32(in+32u+4u*i); c->tag[i]=in[204u+i]; }\r\n    return cal_validate(c);\r\n}\r\nbool cal_complete(const calibration_t *c, const settings_t *s)\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i, banks;\r\n    if(cal_validate(c)!=RES_OK || set_validate(s)!=RES_OK) return false;\r\n    banks=s->board_type==40?6u:(uint8_t)(s->channel_count/8u);\r\n    if(c->bank_count!=banks) return false;\r\n    for(i=0;i<banks;++i) if(c->ref_ppm[i]==CAL_MISSING) return false;\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) if(s->ch[i].type!=CH_TYPE_OFF) {\r\n        /* PT100 calibration/tag format is not specified; fail closed until F0-40. */\r\n        if(s->ch[i].type==CH_TYPE_PT100 || c->baseline_nV[i]==CAL_MISSING ||\r\n           c->tag[i]!=(uint8_t)((s->ch[i].type_epoch<<2)|(uint8_t)s->ch[i].type)) return false;\r\n    }\r\n    return true;\r\n}\r\nres_t cal_learn(calibration_t *c, const settings_t *s, const int32_t baseline_nV[MAX_CHANNELS])\r\n{\r\n    uint8_t i;\r\n    if(cal_validate(c)!=RES_OK || set_validate(s)!=RES_OK || baseline_nV==NULL) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) if(s->ch[i].type!=CH_TYPE_OFF &&\r\n        (s->ch[i].type==CH_TYPE_PT100 || baseline_nV[i]<1500000 || baseline_nV[i]>10000000)) return RES_ERR_RANGE;\r\n    for(i=0;i<s->channel_count;++i) if(s->ch[i].type!=CH_TYPE_OFF) {\r\n        c->baseline_nV[i]=baseline_nV[i];\r\n        c->tag[i]=(uint8_t)((s->ch[i].type_epoch<<2)|(uint8_t)s->ch[i].type);\r\n    }\r\n    return RES_OK;\r\n}\r\n#include \"core_test.h\"\r\n\r\nstatic void record_rules(void)\r\n{\r\n    settings_t s=fixture_settings(), out, bad;\r\n    uint8_t raw[SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE], corrupt[SETTINGS_SLOT_SIZE];\r\n    uint16_t i;\r\n    CHECK(set_validate(&s)==RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(set_pack(&s,raw)==RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(raw[0]==0x54 && raw[1]==0x53 && raw[2]==1 && raw[3]==24);\r\n    CHECK(raw[6]==7 && raw[12]==0x34 && raw[13]==0x12);\r\n    CHECK(set_unpack(raw,24,24,&out)==RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(out.sequence==s.sequence && out.ch[0].trip_dC==1000);\r\n    /* Every serialized field, including reserved header bytes and CRC. */\r\n    for (i=0; i<402; ++i) {\r\n        memcpy(corrupt,raw,sizeof(raw)); corrupt[i]^=0x80;\r\n        CHECK(set_unpack(corrupt,24,24,&out)!=RES_OK);\r\n    }\r\n    CHECK(set_unpack(raw,8,8,&out)!=RES_OK);\r\n#define BAD(field,value) do { bad=s; bad.field=value; CHECK(set_validate(&bad)!=RES_OK); } while(0)\r\n    BAD(board_type,25); BAD(channel_count,23); BAD(address,0); BAD(address,248);\r\n    BAD(baud,2); BAD(pin_bcd,0xA000); BAD(pin_bcd,0x0A00); BAD(pin_bcd,0x00A0); BAD(pin_bcd,0x000A);\r\n    BAD(ch[0].type,(ch_type_t)99); BAD(ch[0].mode,(ch_mode_t)99);\r\n    BAD(ch[0].name[0],0x1F); BAD(ch[0].name[5],0x7F);\r\n    BAD(ch[0].alarm_dC,-1); BAD(ch[0].alarm_dC,1000); BAD(ch[0].trip_dC,0);\r\n    BAD(ch[0].trip_dC,12001); BAD(ch[0].probe_limit_dC,13721);\r\n    BAD(ch[0].band_C,1); BAD(ch[0].band_C,51); BAD(ch[0].type_epoch,64);\r\n    BAD(ch[0].type,CH_TYPE_PT100); BAD(ch[0].type,CH_TYPE_OFF);\r\n    BAD(ch[1].mode,CH_MODE_ALARM_ONLY); BAD(ch[1].alarm_dC,1); BAD(ch[1].trip_dC,1);\r\n    BAD(ch[1].probe_limit_dC,1); BAD(ch[1].band_C,3);\r\n#undef BAD\r\n    bad=s; bad.ch[0].type=CH_TYPE_J; bad.ch[0].probe_limit_dC=12001; CHECK(set_validate(&bad)!=RES_OK);\r\n    bad=s; CHECK(set_change_type(&bad.ch[0],CH_TYPE_OFF)==RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(set_validate(&bad)!=RES_OK); /* at least one fitted channel */\r\n    bad.ch[0].type_epoch=63; CHECK(set_change_type(&bad.ch[0],CH_TYPE_J)==RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(bad.ch[0].type_epoch==0 && bad.ch[0].trip_dC==0 && bad.ch[0].probe_limit_dC==0);\r\n    CHECK(set_validate(&bad)!=RES_OK); /* actual limits must be re-entered */\r\n    bad=s; bad.board_type=40; bad.channel_count=43;\r\n    bad.ch[40]=s.ch[0]; bad.ch[40].type=CH_TYPE_PT100; bad.ch[40].probe_limit_dC=4000;\r\n    CHECK(set_validate(&bad)==RES_OK);\r\n    bad.ch[40].type=CH_TYPE_K; CHECK(set_validate(&bad)!=RES_OK);\r\n    bad=s; bad.board_type=8; bad.channel_count=8; bad.address=247; bad.baud=1; bad.pin_bcd=0x9999;\r\n    bad.ch[0].name[0]=' '; bad.ch[0].name[5]='~'; bad.ch[0].type_epoch=63;\r\n    bad.ch[0].band_C=50; bad.ch[0].alarm_dC=0; bad.ch[0].trip_dC=1;\r\n    CHECK(set_pack(&bad,corrupt)==RES_OK && set_unpack(corrupt,8,8,&out)==RES_OK);\r\n    bad=s; bad.board_type=40; bad.channel_count=43;\r\n    CHECK(set_pack(&bad,corrupt)==RES_OK && set_unpack(corrupt,40,43,&out)==RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(corrupt[706]==0 && corrupt[767]==0);\r\n    CHECK(set_crc16((const uint8_t *)\"123456789\",9)==0x29B1);\r\n    CHECK(set_select(true,1,true,2)==1); CHECK(set_select(true,2,true,1)==0);\r\n    CHECK(set_select(true,0,true,UINT32_MAX)==0); CHECK(set_select(true,UINT32_MAX,true,0)==1);\r\n    CHECK(set_select(true,1,false,2)==0); CHECK(set_select(false,1,true,2)==1);\r\n    CHECK(set_select(false,1,false,2)==-1); CHECK(set_select(true,1,true,1)==0);\r\n    CHECK(set_select(true,0,true,0x80000000u)==0);\r\n    bad=s; bad.ch[0].name[0]='X'; CHECK(!set_protection_changed(&s,&bad));\r\n    bad.ch[0].trip_dC++; CHECK(set_protection_changed(&s,&bad));\r\n}\r\nstatic void calibration_power_cuts(void)\r\n{\r\n    calibration_t old=fixture_cal(), next, a, b;\r\n    set_store_t st; ee_op_t op;\r\n    uint8_t ee[4096], read=0, expected[CAL_SLOT_SIZE];\r\n    unsigned step, writes=0; bool av, bv; int selected;\r\n    old.sequence=4; old.ref_ppm[0]=CAL_MISSING; next=old; next.ref_ppm[0]=100;\r\n    memset(ee,0xFF,sizeof(ee)); CHECK(cal_pack(&old,ee+0x640)==RES_OK);\r\n    set_store_init(&st); CHECK(cal_commit(&st,&next,old.sequence,0)==RES_OK);\r\n    memcpy(expected,st.image,CAL_SLOT_SIZE);\r\n    for(step=0;step<1500 && st.phase!=STORE_DONE;++step) {\r\n        av=cal_unpack(ee+0x640,3,&a)==RES_OK; bv=cal_unpack(ee+0x740,3,&b)==RES_OK;\r\n        selected=set_select(av,a.sequence,bv,b.sequence); CHECK(selected>=0);\r\n        if(selected==0) CHECK(a.sequence==4 && a.ref_ppm[0]==CAL_MISSING);\r\n        if(selected==1) CHECK(memcmp(ee+0x740,expected,249)==0);\r\n        set_store_step(&st,true,true,read,&op);\r\n        if(op.kind==EE_WRITE) { ee[op.address]=op.value; ++writes; }\r\n        if(op.kind==EE_READ) read=ee[op.address];\r\n    }\r\n    CHECK(st.phase==STORE_DONE && writes==250 && st.active_slot==1);\r\n    CHECK(cal_unpack(ee+0x740,3,&b)==RES_OK && b.ref_ppm[0]==100 && b.sequence==5);\r\n}\r\nstatic void calibration_rules(void)\r\n{\r\n    settings_t s=fixture_settings(); calibration_t c=fixture_cal(), d;\r\n    uint8_t raw[CAL_SLOT_SIZE], corrupt[CAL_SLOT_SIZE]; int32_t learned[MAX_CHANNELS]={0};\r\n    uint16_t i;\r\n    CHECK(cal_validate(&c)==RES_OK && cal_complete(&c,&s));\r\n    CHECK(cal_pack(&c,raw)==RES_OK && cal_unpack(raw,3,&d)==RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(d.baseline_nV[0]==3200000 && d.tag[0]==1);\r\n    for(i=0;i<249;++i) {\r\n        memcpy(corrupt,raw,sizeof(raw)); corrupt[i]^=1;\r\n        CHECK(cal_unpack(corrupt,3,&d)!=RES_OK);\r\n    }\r\n    raw[247]^=1; CHECK(cal_unpack(raw,3,&d)!=RES_OK);\r\n    CHECK(cal_unpack(raw,2,&d)!=RES_OK);\r\n    c.ref_ppm[0]=CAL_MISSING; CHECK(cal_validate(&c)==RES_OK && !cal_complete(&c,&s));\r\n    c.ref_ppm[0]=10001; CHECK(cal_validate(&c)!=RES_OK); c.ref_ppm[0]=-10001; CHECK(cal_validate(&c)!=RES_OK);\r\n    c=fixture_cal(); c.ref_ppm[3]=1; CHECK(cal_validate(&c)!=RES_OK);\r\n    c=fixture_cal(); c.baseline_nV[0]=CAL_MISSING; c.tag[0]=0;\r\n    CHECK(cal_validate(&c)==RES_OK && !cal_complete(&c,&s));\r\n    c=fixture_cal(); c.tag[0]=2; CHECK(!cal_complete(&c,&s));\r\n    c=fixture_cal(); s.ch[0].type_epoch=1; CHECK(!cal_complete(&c,&s));\r\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:66:    set_store_init(&st); CHECK(cal_commit(&st,&next,old.sequence,0)==RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:67:    memcpy(expected,st.image,CAL_SLOT_SIZE);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:121:    CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)==RES_OK && st.protection_change);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:129:    b=a; b.ch[0].name[0]='X'; CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)==RES_OK && !st.protection_change);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:135:    b=a; b.ch[0].trip_dC=1100; CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)==RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:139:    { calibration_t c=fixture_cal(); CHECK(cal_commit(&st,&c,9,1)==RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:142:    CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)==RES_BUSY);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:145:    b=a; b.ch[0].trip_dC=1100; CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)==RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:153:    b=a; b.ch[0].type=CH_TYPE_J; CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)!=RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:154:    b.ch[0].type_epoch=1; CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)==RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:155:    b=a; b.ch[0].type_epoch=1; CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,0)!=RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:156:    b=a; CHECK(set_commit(&st,&b,&a,2)!=RES_OK);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:216:        CHECK(set_commit(&st,&next,&old,(uint8_t)settings_slot)==RES_ERR_RANGE);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:217:        CHECK(set_commit_with_cal(&st,&next,&old,(uint8_t)settings_slot,NULL,(uint8_t)cal_slot)==RES_ERR_RANGE);\nfirmware/family/test/unit/test_settings.c:218:        CHECK(set_commit_with_cal(&st,&next,&old,(uint8_t)settings_slot,&cal,2)==RES_ERR_RANGE);\nfirmware/family/