{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content firmware/spec/02-hardware-interface.md | Select-Object -Skip 40 -First 70; Get-Content firmware/family/test/integration/avr_mcal_cycles.c; Get-Content firmware/family/build.ps1 | Select-Object -First 60; git status --short'","aggregated_output":"| PA1 | LCD_E | O | floating | 0 | |\r\n| PA2 | REFOK | I | driven by U404 reverse ch. (push-pull) | input, no pull-up | **active low**: low = engine wire connected; high = broken **or island unpowered** (isolator default-high, `c_iso.py` U408 note) |\r\n| PA3 | REFTEST | O | floating -> U405 input open | 0 | high = self-test (Q401 pulls REF_SENSE low). **OPEN-H1:** CA-IS3761 output state with its input *floating* (MCU in reset) is not in the local text; if it defaults high, REFOK reads \"broken\" during MCU reset - harmless (RUN is off) |\r\n| PA4-PA7 | LCD_D4-D7 | O | floating | 0 | |\r\n| PB0 | CS_ADC2 | O | high (R431 10k to +5V) | 1 | bank B AD7124, via U403 |\r\n| PB1 | CS_ADC3 | O | high (R432) | 1 | bank C AD7124, via U403. CKOUT fuse must stay unprogrammed (section 6) |\r\n| PB2 | CS_CJ1 | O | high (R433) | 1 | bank A TMP126 #1, via U404 |\r\n| PB3 | RUN_PERMIT | O (OC0A) | floating; R702 100k holds the trip gate low -> relay off | 0, Timer0 off | charge-pump drive, section 4.2. A static level never holds the relay (`c_out.py` pump note) |\r\n| PB4 | CS_ADC1 | O | high (R430) | 1 | bank A AD7124. **Also the SPI /SS pin**: must be an output before SPE/MSTR are set (AVR 18.3) |\r\n| PB5 | MOSI | O | floating | 0 | SPI and TMP126 bit-bang data out; also ISP |\r\n| PB6 | MISO | I | via R405 2k2 from U403 reverse ch. | input, no pull-up | ISP contention resistor R405 |\r\n| PB7 | SCK | O | floating | **1** | SPI mode 3 idles high (section 3) |\r\n| PC0 | CS_CJ2 | O | high (R434) | 1 | bank A TMP126 #2 |\r\n| PC1 | CS_CJ3 | O | high (R435) | 1 | bank B TMP126 #1 |\r\n| PC2 | RUN_SENSE | I | R703 10k from coil low side, 100 nF | input, no pull-up | low = trip relay coil energised. JTAG TCK pin: JTAGEN fuse off + MCUCR.JTD (section 6, 8) |\r\n| PC3 | CS_CJ4 | O | high (R436) | 1 | bank B TMP126 #2; JTAG TMS |\r\n| PC4 | CS_CJ5 | O | high (R437) | 1 | bank C TMP126 #1; JTAG TDO |\r\n| PC5 | CS_CJ6 | O | high (R438) | 1 | bank C TMP126 #2 (via U405); JTAG TDI |\r\n| PC6 | ALARM_DRIVE | O | floating; R712 100k gate pull-down -> alarm relay off | 0 | relay energised when high. Polarity meaning (energised = no alarm?) is `04`'s (0043 3.5, \"to confirm in F0\") |\r\n| PC7 | ALARM_SENSE | I | R713 10k from coil low side | input, no pull-up | low = alarm coil energised |\r\n| PD0 | UART_RX (RXD0) | I | R738 10k pull-up (ADM2587E RxD is high-Z while transmitting) | USART0 | |\r\n| PD1 | UART_TX (TXD0) | O | floating | USART0 | |\r\n| PD2 | BTN_UP | I-PU | floating | pull-up | active low. UP and DOWN low together = ESC (D41 D3, D501/D502) |\r\n| PD3 | BTN_DOWN | I-PU | floating | pull-up | active low |\r\n| PD4 | BTN_SET | I-PU | floating | pull-up | active low |\r\n| PD5 | SIO_WR_N | O | high (R439 10k; island side R445 10k) | 1 | low = U411 drives DIN onto TMP126 SIO (D41 D1). **Never low while an AD7124 CS is low** |\r\n| PD6 | BTN_ACK | I-PU | floating | pull-up | active low |\r\n| PD7 | RS485_DE | O | low (R737 10k pull-down) = receive | 0 | DE and /RE tied (R733) |\r\n| RESET | RESET_N | - | R501 10k, C508 10n | - | ISP J501 pin 5 |\r\n| XTAL1/2 | 8 MHz crystal | - | Y501, 22 pF C0G | - | fuses section 6 |\r\n| AREF | AREF | - | 100 nF | - | AVR ADC not used |\r\n\r\nESC on the 24-ch has no pin: ESC = BTN_UP and BTN_DOWN both low (C 8.5: pin reads ~0.6 V vs VIL max 1.5 V).\r\n\r\n### 1.2 8-ch REV B0 (source FAM `B8`: MCU24 with PC1 = SIO_WR_N and unused CS removed; D39 notes)\r\n\r\nSame as 1.1 except:\r\n\r\n| Pin | Signal | Dir | Reset state | Init | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| PB0 | - (unused) | I-PU | floating | pull-up | AVR 14.2.6 recommends the internal pull-up on unconnected pins |\r\n| PB1 | - (unused) | I-PU | floating | pull-up | |\r\n| PB2 | CS_CJ1 | O | high (R433) | 1 | TMP126 #1 via U403 |\r\n| PB4 | CS_ADC1 | O | high (R430) | 1 | /SS: output before SPI enable |\r\n| PC0 | CS_CJ2 | O | high (R434) | 1 | TMP126 #2 via U403 |\r\n| PC1 | SIO_WR_N | O | high (R439) | 1 | via U404 |\r\n| PC3, PC4, PC5 | - (unused) | I-PU | floating | pull-up | JTAG pins: JTAG off still required |\r\n| PD5 | BTN_ESC | I-PU | floating | pull-up | own ESC pin (no diodes, `esc_diodes=False`); UP+DOWN chord also = ESC (0043 6) |\r\n\r\nIsolators: U403 forward SCK, MOSI, CS_ADC1, CS_CJ1, CS_CJ2; reverse DOUT -> MISO. U404 forward REFTEST,\r\nSIO_WR_N; reverse REFOK.\r\n\r\n### 1.3 40-ch REV A0 (source FAM `B40` / `MCU40`; D39 D3 and notes)\r\n\r\nSame as 1.1 except:\r\n\r\n| Pin | Signal | Dir | Reset state | Init | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| PB0 | CSA0 | O | floating (no pull-up) | 0 | 74HC154 A0 via U403. Address lines are don't-care while CS_EN is high |\r\n| PB1 | CSA1 | O | floating | 0 | A1 via U403 |\r\n| PB2 | CSA2 | O | floating | 0 | A2 via U403 |\r\n| PC0 | CSA3 | O | floating | 0 | A3 via U404 - **a different port from A0-A2**, so an address change is never atomic: change it only while CS_EN is high |\r\n| PB4 | CS_EN | O | high (R430 10k control side; R444 10k island side) | **1 first, then DDR** (D39: \"drive high before making it an output\") | 74HC154 E0 (E1 tied to GND_ISO). High = every Y output high = all devices deselected. Also /SS |\r\n| PC1 | SIO_WR_N | O | high (R439) | 1 | via U404 |\r\n| PC3, PC4, PC5 | - (unused) | I-PU | floating | pull-up | |\r\n| PD5 | BTN_ESC | I-PU | floating | pull-up | |\r\n\r\nDecoder outputs (FAM `c_iso.py decoder()`): Y0-Y4 = AD7124 of banks A-E, Y5 = RTD AD7124, Y6-Y15 = TMP126 1-10\r\nwhere TMP126 j of bank b (b = 1..5, i = 0,1) is j = 2(b-1)+i+1, i.e. bank A = Y6/Y7, B = Y8/Y9, C = Y10/Y11,\r\nD = Y12/Y13, E = Y14/Y15. Address = Yn number, A0 = LSB.\r\n/* Cycle calibration of the unmodified target MCAL in GNU's AVR simulator.\r\n * Hardware registers are RAM in this simulator; explicitly set input levels. */\r\n#include \"mcal/gpio.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/spi.h\"\r\n#include \"mcal/timer.h\"\r\n#include \"drivers/keys.h\"\r\n#include <avr/io.h>\r\nvolatile uint8_t cycle_kind,cycle_value;\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void cycle_begin(void) { __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void cycle_end(void) { __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void cycle_done(void) { for(;;) __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\nvoid TIMER2_COMPA_vect(void);\r\nint main(void) {\r\n    uint16_t i; gpio_init(); timer_init(); keys_init();\r\n    PINA=PINB=PINC=PIND=255;\r\n    for(i=0;i<256;i++) {\r\n        cycle_value=(uint8_t)i; cycle_kind=9;\r\n        cycle_begin(); (void)spi_soft_xfer((uint8_t)i); cycle_end();\r\n    }\r\n    cycle_kind=2; cycle_begin(); gpio_write(PIN(PORT_D,7),true); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=3; cycle_begin(); (void)gpio_read(PIN(PORT_D,7)); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=4; cycle_begin(); gpio_mask(PORT_A,255,255); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=5; cycle_begin(); delay_us(49); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=11; cycle_begin(); (void)tick_ms(); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=13; cycle_begin(); (void)timer_run_start_at(900,tick_ms()); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=15; cycle_begin(); (void)timer_run_remaining(); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=16; cycle_begin(); (void)timer_run_active(); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_kind=32; cycle_begin(); TIMER2_COMPA_vect(); cycle_end();\r\n    cycle_done();\r\n}\r\nparam([switch]$HostOnly,[switch]$AvrOnly)\r\n$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'\r\n$root=$PSScriptRoot\r\n$out=Join-Path $root 'build'\r\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force $out | Out-Null\r\nStart-Transcript -Path (Join-Path $out 'validation.log') -Force | Out-Null\r\nfunction Run([string]$file,[string[]]$a) {\r\n    & $file @a 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { Write-Host \"$_\" }\r\n    if($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"$file failed ($LASTEXITCODE)\" }\r\n}\r\nfunction Sources([string]$name) {\r\n    Get-Content (Join-Path $root \"sources/$name.txt\") | ForEach-Object {\r\n        $s=($_ -replace '#.*','').Trim()\r\n        if($s) { Join-Path $root $s }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\nif(-not $AvrOnly) {\r\n    $vswhere='C:/Program Files (x86)/Microsoft Visual Studio/Installer/vswhere.exe'\r\n    $vs=& $vswhere -latest -products '*' -requires Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Tools.x86.x64 -property installationPath\r\n    if(-not $vs) { throw 'MSVC build tools missing' }\r\n    $dev=Join-Path $vs 'Common7/Tools/VsDevCmd.bat'\r\n    $src=@(Sources 'hardware_host')\r\n    $quoted=($src | ForEach-Object { '\"'+$_+'\"' }) -join ' '\r\n    # hardware_host includes the real F1 shell and register-fake integration\r\n    # scenarios; the obsolete F0 \"ACK cannot grant RUN\" test is superseded.\r\n    $exe=Join-Path $out 'test_hardware.exe'\r\n    $installer=Split-Path $vswhere\r\n    $cmd=\"set `\"PATH=$installer;%PATH%`\" && call `\"$dev`\" -arch=x64 -no_logo && cl /nologo /std:c11 /W4 /WX /O2 /fsanitize=address /Zi /DFAMILY_TEST /D_CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS /I`\"$root/include`\" /I`\"$root/test/fakes`\" $quoted /Fe:`\"$exe`\" /Fo:`\"$out/`\" /Fd:`\"$out/hardware.pdb`\"\"\r\n    Run $env:ComSpec @('/d','/s','/c',$cmd)\r\n    Run $env:ComSpec @('/d','/s','/c',\"set `\"PATH=$installer;%PATH%`\" && call `\"$dev`\" -arch=x64 -no_logo && `\"$exe`\"\")\r\n    $timerExe=Join-Path $out 'test_timer.exe'\r\n    $cmd=\"set `\"PATH=$installer;%PATH%`\" && call `\"$dev`\" -arch=x64 -no_logo && cl /nologo /std:c11 /W4 /WX /O2 /I`\"$root/test/stubs`\" /I`\"$root/include`\" `\"$root/src/mcal/timer.c`\" `\"$root/test/integration/test_timer.c`\" /Fe:`\"$timerExe`\" /Fo:`\"$out/`\"\"\r\n    Run $env:ComSpec @('/d','/s','/c',$cmd)\r\n    Run $timerExe @()\r\n}\r\nif(-not $HostOnly) {\r\n    $bin='C:/Program Files (x86)/Labcenter Electronics/Proteus 8 Professional/Tools/ARDUINO/hardware/tools/avr/bin'\r\n    $gcc=Join-Path $bin 'avr-gcc.exe'\r\n    $stackHeader=Get-Content (Join-Path $root 'include/app/stack_budget.h') -Raw\r\n    $stackBytes=[int]([regex]::Match($stackHeader,'#define APP_STACK_BYTES (\\d+)u').Groups[1].Value)\r\n    if($stackBytes -lt 1024) { throw 'Stack reservation missing/too small' }\r\n    # The existing pure commit owns a settings + calibration working copy.\r\n    # Keep the shell canary below that frame plus caller/interrupt margin.\r\n    $stackObj=Join-Path $out 'settings_stack.o'\r\n    Run $gcc @('-std=c11','-Os','-Wall','-Wextra','-Werror','-mmcu=atmega1284p',\"-I$root/include\",'-fstack-usage','-c',(Join-Path $root 'src/services/settings_store.c'),'-o',$stackObj)\r\n    $frames=Get-Content (Join-Path $out 'settings_stack.su') | ForEach-Object {\r\n        if($_ -match '\\t(\\d+)\\t') { [int]$Matches[1] }\r\n    }\r\n    $maxFrame=($frames | Measure-Object -Maximum).Maximum\r\n    if(-not $maxFrame -or $maxFrame+384 -gt $stackBytes) { throw \"Commit stack frame $maxFrame + 384 margin exceeds $stackBytes\" }\r\n    Write-Host \"AVR commit frame: $maxFrame bytes; caller/interrupt margin: 384; stack reservation: $stackBytes\"\r\n    $elf=Join-Path $out 'thermo24_f1.elf'\r\n    $flags=@('-std=c11','-Os','-Wall','-Wextra','-Werror','-mmcu=atmega1284p','-DF_CPU=8000000UL',\"-I$root/include\",'-ffunction-sections','-fdata-sections','-Wl,--gc-sections,--section-start=.image_crc=0x1FFFE,--undefined=image_crc')\r\n    Run $gcc ($flags+@(Sources 'hardware_avr')+@('-o',$elf))\r\n    $objcopy=Join-Path $bin 'avr-objcopy.exe'\r\n    $raw=Join-Path $out 'image.bin'\r\n    Run $objcopy @('-O','binary','-j','.text','-j','.data',$elf,$raw)\r\n    $endLine=& (Join-Path $bin 'avr-nm.exe') '--defined-only' $elf | Select-String ' __data_load_end$'\r\n    if(-not $endLine) { throw '__data_load_end missing' }\r\n    $end=[Convert]::ToInt32(($endLine.ToString() -split '\\s+')[0],16)\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
