{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content firmware/family/test/integration/avr_mcal_wrap.c | Select-Object -Skip 68 -First 18; Get-Content firmware/family/include/services/fault.h; Get-Content firmware/family/test/integration/README.md -Tail 40'","aggregated_output":"__attribute__((noinline)) void profile_io_begin(void) { __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\n__attribute__((noinline)) void profile_io_end(void) { __asm__ volatile(\"nop\"); }\r\nstatic void enter(uint8_t kind,uint16_t arg) {\r\n    if(depth++==0) { profile_kind=kind; profile_arg=arg; profile_io_begin(); }\r\n}\r\nstatic void leave(void) { if(--depth==0) profile_io_end(); }\r\n#define WRAPPER __attribute__((noinline,optimize(\"no-optimize-sibling-calls\")))\r\n#define RET(t,n,a,c,k,p) WRAPPER t n a { t result; enter(k,p); result=base_##n c; leave(); return result; }\r\n#define VOID(n,a,c,k,p) WRAPPER void n a { enter(k,p); base_##n c; leave(); }\r\nVOID(gpio_init,(void),(),1,0)\r\nVOID(gpio_write,(pin_t p,bool h),(p,h),2,p)\r\nRET(bool,gpio_read,(pin_t p),(p),3,p)\r\nVOID(gpio_mask,(uint8_t p,uint8_t m,uint8_t v),(p,m,v),4,p)\r\nVOID(delay_us,(uint16_t u),(u),5,u)\r\nVOID(spi_init,(void),(),6,0)\r\nVOID(spi_enable,(bool e),(e),7,0)\r\nRET(res_t,spi_xfer,(uint8_t t,uint8_t *r),(t,r),8,0)\r\nRET(uint8_t,spi_soft_xfer,(uint8_t t),(t),9,0)\r\n#ifndef FAMILY_FAULT_H\r\n#define FAMILY_FAULT_H\r\n#include \"common/types.h\"\r\n#include \"common/fault_codes.h\"\r\n#define FAULT_CODES 52u\r\n#define FAULT_UNITS 96u\r\n#define FAULT_BYTES (FAULT_UNITS / 8u)\r\ntypedef enum { ACT_NONE=0, ACT_ALARM=1, ACT_TRIP=3 } act_t;\r\ntypedef struct {\r\n    uint8_t active[FAULT_CODES][FAULT_BYTES];\r\n    uint8_t latch[FAULT_CODES][FAULT_BYTES];\r\n    bool internal;\r\n} fault_registry_t;\r\nvoid fault_init(fault_registry_t *r);\r\n/* True on a new activation; invalid codes/units raise an internal trip.\r\n * C-code units consumed by protection are zero-based CHANNELS (also C03).\r\n * Preserve raw CM pin identity separately when constructing its event. */\r\nbool fault_raise(fault_registry_t *r, fault_code_t code, uint8_t unit);\r\nvoid fault_clear(fault_registry_t *r, fault_code_t code, uint8_t unit);\r\nbool fault_active(const fault_registry_t *r, fault_code_t code);\r\nbool fault_at(const fault_registry_t *r, fault_code_t code, uint8_t unit);\r\nact_t fault_action(fault_code_t code, ch_mode_t mode);\r\nbool fault_trip_active(const fault_registry_t *r);\r\nfault_code_t fault_first_trip(const fault_registry_t *r,uint8_t *unit); /* byte search; G/B only */\r\nbool fault_alarm_latched(const fault_registry_t *r);\r\n/* Settings-aware consumers combine G/B latches with fitted-channel C latches. */\r\nbool fault_global_alarm_latched(const fault_registry_t *r);\r\nbool fault_latched_at(const fault_registry_t *r, fault_code_t code, uint8_t unit);\r\n/* Clears only inactive causes; internal input corruption requires reset. */\r\nvoid fault_ack(fault_registry_t *r);\r\n#endif\r\nfor all 256 transmitted byte values; the actual Timer2 ISR is calibrated too.\r\nThe simulator needs its ELF architecture corrected from avr:51 to avr:5 to use\r\nthe ATmega1284P's two-byte PC, and `.data` restored after startup because it does\r\nnot load that section's flash LMA. Neither workaround changes instruction bytes.\r\nThe profiler aliases EEPROM A/B fixture slots to fit SRAM; power-cut correctness\r\nbelongs to the independent full-EEPROM host suite, not this timing harness.\r\nRaw cycles, per-pass estimates and calibration results are in `build/profile/`.\r\nThe sampled full-pass estimate reserves 25% + 2048 cycles for interrupts and is\r\nnot an exhaustive WCET proof. It exceeds the 64000-cycle (8 ms) budget.\r\nThe final sampled maximum is 334015 cycles / 41.752 ms, with epoch-wrap commit\r\nand CJ read in the same pass: 159463 production CPU cycles + 106110 MCAL bound,\r\nthen the interrupt reserve. Pure epoch-wrap commit alone is 109606 cycles /\r\n13.7007 ms. The calibration measures Timer2 ISR execution at 716 cycles.\r\n\r\nS3 remains blocked by protected sources: `set_commit_with_cal()` alone measures\r\n76044 cycles (9.5055 ms), and `src/mcal/spi.c` software SPI measures 3234 cycles\r\nper byte (97020 cycles / 12.1275 ms for a normal 30-byte CJ read). Both violate\r\n`01` section 2 before other loop work. Neither protected file was changed.\r\nAllowed CPU reductions include byte searches, one validation per pass, an\r\nincremental event-ring recovery/cached cursor, bounded service EEPROM CRC work,\r\nincremental mutable ADC verification, and removal of LCD modulo division.\r\n\r\nProduction file inventory (relative to `firmware/family`):\r\n\r\n- `src/app/{main,app,protection,ack_input,ee_owner,service}.c`;\r\n  `include/app/{protection,outputs_hw,acquisition_budget}.h`.\r\n- `src/drivers/{keys,relays,ad7124,lcd}.c`, `include/drivers/keys.h`;\r\n  `src/mcal/timer.c`, `include/mcal/timer.h`;\r\n  `src/services/{fault,scan}.c`, `include/services/fault.h`.\r\n- Small permitted integration exceptions: relay handoff checks expiry atomically;\r\n  service adds press abort and chunks EEPROM CRC; ADC/scan split the final mutable\r\n  verification without weakening its checks, retaining ID/transport classification;\r\n  LCD cursor increment avoids repeated AVR division.\r\n\r\nSupport changes: `build.ps1`, `sources/hardware_host.txt`,\r\n`test/unit/{test_peripherals,test_protection}.c`,\r\n`test/integration/{README.md,model.c,model.h,test_app.c,test_review.c,test_timer.c,\r\navr_profile.c,avr_mcal_wrap.c,avr_mcal_cycles.c,profile_avr.ps1,profile_summary.py}`,\r\nand `test/stubs/{settings_counted.c,avr/io.h,avr/interrupt.h,util/atomic.h}`.\r\nNo acceptance, common-header, settings/event/TC-core source was edited.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
